	('0c6c53a9-c040-411d-a09e-ba80b8419d9e', 'Sarah', 'McGuire', 'Hello! I’m originally from Rye, New York, but I moved to Lake Tahoe in 2001. For years, I worked as a traveling waitress before deciding in 2009 to return to school and pursue my lifelong passion for science—without knowing exactly where it would take me.

From 2011 to 2014, I studied biology at Humboldt State University, focusing on bacteriology and botany. I then attended UNR in Reno for graduate school as a research scientist. However, after a challenging (yet ultimately fortunate) conflict with my advisor, I decided to leave research. That pivotal moment led me to pursue my M.Ed., a decision that shaped me into the science teacher I am today.  ', '  I am in my 5th year of teaching which has included 2 years of High School Biology, 1 year of Middle School Math, and now in my 2nd year of HS Chemistry. ', '{Chemistry,Biology}', '{Chemistry,Biology}', NULL, '2025-03-11 21:05:37.25349+00', '2025-05-06 16:39:59.583919+00', '{"{\"name\": \"Chemistry Teacher\", \"status\": \"active\"}"}', 'smcguire@ttusd.org', '{"chat_notifications": true}', NULL, NULL, 'active', NULL, true, NULL, '{"sms": false, "email": true, "in_app": true}', false, NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL, NULL),
