	('e703c834-b010-4c88-9b89-e310df8ad353', 'Jason', 'Fernandez', 'Jason Fernandez holds a Master’s degree in General Psychology with a concentration in Industrial-Organizational Psychology, as well as a Master’s in Social Work. He is a Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW) in the state of Texas.

He is the founder and owner of 60 Watts of Clarity®, an AI literacy platform dedicated to empowering educators and communities through ethical, accessible technology. Jason also serves as an AI Technology Consultant at a major public university, where he supports the integration of artificial intelligence into higher education through a focus on human-centered design, emotional intelligence, and digital dignity.

He is the creator of the Belonging-Based Bot Design System™, a trademarked framework that embeds trauma-informed values, emotional awareness, and cultural competence into AI agents.

Jason was recently accepted into the PhD program in Social Work at the University of Texas at Arlington, where his research explores the psychosocial impacts of artificial intelligence on human relationships, identity, and systems of care.

🛠 How to Use This Version:', 'Jason has over 13 years of teaching experience in higher education, primarily in the discipline of psychology at the community college level. His teaching portfolio includes courses in general psychology, lifespan development, and human behavior, with a strong emphasis on culturally responsive pedagogy and learner-centered practices.

He currently teaches in the Graduate College of Social Work, where he facilitates instruction on equity, trauma-informed care, organizational systems, and ethical practice. His approach is grounded in social work values and informed by years of direct clinical experience in hospice care.

As an AI Technology Consultant, Jason also leads faculty workshops and learning sessions on AI literacy, bias mitigation, digital ethics, and emotionally intelligent integration of AI tools in education. His teaching blends psychological insight, social work ethics, and technical fluency to meet the complex needs of today’s learners.

