sks and problems or projects.\",\"startTime\":1740788338,\"endTime\":1740788343},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Whatever they are.\",\"startTime\":1740788343,\"endTime\":1740788345},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Where we''re using AI as a tool and it''s pushing our boundary that zone approximal development. \",\"startTime\":1740788345,\"endTime\":1740788351},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And we as learners are being challenged to think critically and use the tools to help us do so, rather than if it''s, if it''s, and that''s got to be the tasks and the challenges or the problems or the assignments or the projects or whatever it is that we''re given to do or take upon ourselves. But if we''re we''re asking \",\"startTime\":1740788352,\"endTime\":1740788370},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740788357,\"endTime\":1740788357},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Yeah, absolutely.\",\"startTime\":1740788358,\"endTime\":1740788359},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"kids, just like today, if we''re asking to do square roots of large numbers and we show them the algorithm by hand, nobody uses that anymore. We use a calculator. \",\"startTime\":1740788370,\"endTime\":1740788379},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"So there''s no.\",\"startTime\":1740788381,\"endTime\":1740788382},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"There''s no discussion today about that one. So we''re just like of course, and \",\"startTime\":1740788383,\"endTime\":1740788387},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"even along the lines of grammar checking and spell checking, we totally trust the spell checker. We don''t go do it by hand anymore and so. \",\"startTime\":1740788387,\"endTime\":1740788394},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Warning about that notion of what are the projects that we''re doing or the tasks or the problems or the things that we''re asking learners to do. So I think the \",\"startTime\":1740788396,\"endTime\":1740788405},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"role of learners in the future, they will have to even ensure on their own self. \",\"startTime\":1740788405,\"endTime\":1740788410},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"That they''re using tools strategically and not.\",\"startTime\":1740788410,\"endTime\":1740788413},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Replacing their tools because.\",\"startTime\":1740788414,\"endTime\":1740788415},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And I''m betting when you''re using AI, at times you''re like, uh, it''s doing more than I know what it''s doing and it''s not really helping ''cause it''s just magic and I don''t know what''s going on. Umm, that''s what I feel sometimes with the \",\"startTime\":1740788416,\"endTime\":1740788425},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Right, right.\",\"startTime\":1740788423,\"endTime\":1740788425},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"AI, Like, uh, I''m like trying to learn about dark matter or something. I have \",\"startTime\":1740788425,\"endTime\":1740788428},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"no idea what''s really going on, but I''m just like overreaching my, my, my, my knowledge base and critical thinking. I''m like, Oh yeah, that''s right, ''cause \",\"startTime\":1740788428,\"endTime\":1740788434},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"it said it. \",\"startTime\":1740788434,\"endTime\":1740788437},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I do agree with you. I do think that learners moving forward are going \",\"startTime\":1740788438,\"endTime\":1740788442},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"to have the opportunity to use these AI tools to then create more than they have been. Like how we are able to create podcasts, we''re able to create faceless \",\"startTime\":1740788442,\"endTime\":1740788450},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"content and AI content and we''re able to just produce so much work instantly. \",\"startTime\":1740788450,\"endTime\":1740788454},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I do think learners are now going to be put in a position where instead 