t\":\"at the thread of the conversation. Why might Jeff not be talking? Well, because \",\"startTime\":1744213940,\"endTime\":1744213944},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"we were like only like giving sports, like basketball metaphors. Jeff doesn''t \",\"startTime\":1744213944,\"endTime\":1744213947},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"know shit about basketball. He can''t like engage in that conversation. So like. \",\"startTime\":1744213947,\"endTime\":1744213951},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Let''s like, let''s go back, let''s pull out a different metaphor. I don''t know. \",\"startTime\":1744213953,\"endTime\":1744213956},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I mean, I think I don''t know if that if I''m making sense or. \",\"startTime\":1744213956,\"endTime\":1744213959},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no, I like that. I like that you''re talking about even in the the facilitation \",\"startTime\":1744213958,\"endTime\":1744213962},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"work, the educator, the teachers role and what they''re doing by calling or not calling on people using the analogies, the types of questions, the whatever it is, what''s in inherent even in my own bias. And then I can use a tool to \",\"startTime\":1744213962,\"endTime\":1744213974},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"help map that out and to trace that down. That sounds like a super reflective \",\"startTime\":1744213974,\"endTime\":1744213978},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"tool. \",\"startTime\":1744213978,\"endTime\":1744213982},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Because we.\",\"startTime\":1744213980,\"endTime\":1744213982},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"We did this pre, you know, class questionnaire and I asked Jeff to share, like, what are some of his interests? And you know, I''m going back, ''cause that''s \",\"startTime\":1744213983,\"endTime\":1744213990},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"data that I''m not pulling up in my head right now because I''m going down this rabbit hole. \",\"startTime\":1744213990,\"endTime\":1744213996},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, by the way, do you know what rabbit hole means? Because like that''s \",\"startTime\":1744213998,\"endTime\":1744214001},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"the Super western like Alice in Wonderland type example of shit. And so like \",\"startTime\":1744214001,\"endTime\":1744214004},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"there''s all these different things that it''s just like really quick connections that your brain can fire. But like if you can also see it, it can really build \",\"startTime\":1744214004,\"endTime\":1744214010},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"community in a dope way. \",\"startTime\":1744214010,\"endTime\":1744214013},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, I like that.\",\"startTime\":1744214014,\"endTime\":1744214016},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Sorry and.\",\"startTime\":1744214017,\"endTime\":1744214018},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"No, don''t be sorry with that. It''s interesting your, your, your take on it was \",\"startTime\":1744214019,\"endTime\":1744214023},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"thinking about the classroom and the conversations happening in the classroom and bias that''s coming up there. And I was thinking that this was biased like \",\"startTime\":1744214023,\"endTime\":1744214031},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"the the result of the GPT because you just put it up there like when you and I were earlier on the computer and I was just like asking it something and then it spits something out and matter of fact, you called it out. \",\"startTime\":1744214031,\"endTime\":1744214042},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"In the result, it said about an equity focus.\",\"startTime\":1744214043,\"endTime\":1744214048},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Go or whatever it was in there and you call that out. And then that was something \",\"startTime\":1744214052,\"endTime\":1744214057},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"that was biased. I thought about the GPT because it had been trained on it. \",\"startTime\":1744214057,\"endTime\":1744214061},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"So I was thinking of like, you''re in class and you know how when you''ve said stuff to the students and then you realize as soon as you said it that way, I''m working with teenagers and that''s not the right way to say it. \",\"startTime\":1744214061,\"endTime\":1744214074},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Like like the one for golfing when I was golfing a ton with my dad, They you''re in a threesome. There''s a threesome in front of us. It''s a group of three. That''s \",\"startTime\":1744214076,\"endTime\":1744214083},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"what just the language there. It''s a threesome. But if you use that in your \",\"startTime\":1744214083,\"endTime\":1744214086},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"high school math class, hey. \",\"startTime\":1744214086,\"endTime\":1744214090},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Sure.\",\"startTime\":1744214090,\"endTime\":1744214091},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Get you into, oh, wait, why don''t you be a threesome over there? That''s not \",\"startTime\":1744214090,\"endTime\":1744214094},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"what you should say to high school kids about that''s just like not gonna work. \",\"startTime\":1744214094,\"endTime\":1744214098},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"So I''m imagining that moment when when it''s the GPT or the AI tool up on the screen says something. \",\"startTime\":1744214098,\"endTime\":1744214106},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"For sure.\",\"startTime\":1744214098,\"endTime\":1744214099},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And all of the kids cringe or half of the kids cringe because they said something about Alison Wonderland type of thing. But it''s obviously it doesn''t fit us \",\"startTime\":1744214107,\"endTime\":1744214115},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"in our community. You''re like wrong. And you''ve seen it with teachers before \",\"startTime\":1744214115,\"endTime\":1744214119},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"when teachers talk and you''re like trying to cover yourself and hide because you don''t want to be in the same place associated because the teacher just said that. Did you really just say that? We''re gonna have to have a talk? That''s \",\"startTime\":1744214119,\"endTime\":1744214130},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"not how you talk about kids. And these kids are not gonna understand what it \",\"startTime\":1744214130,\"endTime\":1744214134},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"is. And kids don''t have a boat to go on. \",\"startTime\":1744214134,\"endTime\":1744214137},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Weekend, So please don''t ask them to think about taking their boat out for a trip this weekend. Like you''re totally biased and missing the mark. So that''s \",\"startTime\":1744214139,\"endTime\":1744214148},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"why I was wondering about and thinking. And so I really appreciate you bringing \",\"startTime\":1744214148,\"endTime\":1744214152},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"it to the practical sense of just that we do things and asking questions and who we pick on creates bias in the conversation. It makes me wonder. Go ahead. \",\"startTime\":1744214152,\"endTime\":1744214160},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Well, oh, no, sorry. Go go ahead. I''ll jump in after.\",\"startTime\":1744214161,\"endTime\":1744214166},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I was just wondering what would you do in the classroom if something like that popped up on the screen, like you did it with your teacher group later today or with students and you''re like, oh, that''s just wrong or that''s really biased? \",\"startTime\":1744214164,\"endTime\":1744214176},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"It''d be fun just to like put it out there because it''s kind of this like.\",\"startTime\":1744214179,\"endTime\":1744214182},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, side by assistant who like it''s not personal. It''s just like from \",\"startTime\":1744214182,\"endTime\":1744214186},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"from the data, from the from the training, from whatever. \",\"startTime\":1744214186,\"endTime\":1744214191},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Coupled with like we were saying something similar, but like have this in a faculty meeting or like an apartment meeting where you''re talking about kids \",\"startTime\":1744214193,\"endTime\":1744214202},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"and the AI system is like listening and be like, hey, you keep repeating the same thing that, you know, why do you keep bringing up, you know, Jeff''s family or Tom''s, you know, like that doesn''t seem, you know, it can also point out like the way you''re talking about kids does not encourage agency. \",\"startTime\":1744214202,\"endTime\":1744214219},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Here''s a question here. Here''s a way to like, go back at it and, you know, get \",\"startTime\":1744214220,\"endTime\":1744214223},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744214222,\"endTime\":1744214224},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"to your goals. \",\"startTime\":1744214223,\"endTime\":1744214225},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Speaking of which, I have a 10:00.\",\"startTime\":1744214228,\"endTime\":1744214230},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I was noticing the time we got to.\",\"startTime\":1744214231,\"endTime\":1744214233},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Marketing and branding meeting.\",\"startTime\":1744214232,\"endTime\":1744214235},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Which is not as fun as this.\",\"startTime\":1744214235,\"endTime\":1744214236},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1744214237,\"endTime\":1744214237},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"All right, let''s hit next. Last card''s a short one. Thanks, Tom. I learned that \",\"startTime\":1744214237,\"endTime\":1744214243},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1744214241,\"endTime\":1744214241},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I can use the AI tools to help map out my own bias and what''s happening in conversations. \",\"startTime\":1744214243,\"endTime\":1744214250},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Rather than just be analyzing the bias of the GPT tool, I can use it effectively to be a coach and the analyst for my my facilitation and my teaching. So thank \",\"startTime\":1744214251,\"endTime\":1744214260},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"you for that. \",\"startTime\":1744214260,\"endTime\":1744214265},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Yes, you''re welcome and thank you and.\",\"startTime\":1744214269,\"endTime\":1744214272},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I think my yeah, I''m, I''m really sticking with this. Like you brought up the \",\"startTime\":1744214273,\"endTime\":1744214276},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"fears, like the first card was about fears. \",\"startTime\":1744214276,\"endTime\":1744214280},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And I think so much of our conversation about fears needs to recognize that the way we''re talking about those fears is actually devaluing teachers and encouraging this. \",\"startTime\":1744214281,\"endTime\":1744214291},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"This narrative that teachers are just supposed to be doing repetitive, simple. \",\"startTime\":1744214291,\"endTime\":1744214297},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And I like, I really appreciate the word simple because that''s, that''s an important word, like if we want kids to be simple and we want teachers to be simple. \",\"startTime\":1744214299,\"endTime\":1744214307},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Then we''re just perpetuating that fear and locking it in.\",\"startTime\":1744214308,\"endTime\":1744214311},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, alright, Tom, you''re amazing. Thanks for this great start to the day.\",\"startTime\":1744214314,\"endTi