ean it''s well informed in these other things. And that''s another \",\"startTime\":1739484035,\"endTime\":1739484039},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484036,\"endTime\":1739484038},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"one that I''ve read in an articles as well, just to give you more clarity to it. But practically same thing is if you don''t have. \",\"startTime\":1739484039,\"endTime\":1739484048},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Specificity when you''re training out your model.\",\"startTime\":1739484049,\"endTime\":1739484052},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And it''s really challenging to make sure you have the knowledge base in the right place. Like we want to be really clear about this is a ChatGPT or is this \",\"startTime\":1739484053,\"endTime\":1739484063},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a, a GPT assistant for the Washington State school principals? \",\"startTime\":1739484063,\"endTime\":1739484068},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484066,\"endTime\":1739484068},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So that they''re aligned to their framework, they''re aligned to Ospi''s menus of best practices, and then take the language around that. But what''s the model \",\"startTime\":1739484068,\"endTime\":1739484076},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"built around and, and what''s it focused on ''cause if it''s just for chat, it can chat, but just know it''s gonna chat like anybody can chat and it''s trained on all this general thing. Yeah, I''m with you too. Very much so. Biased Bias, \",\"startTime\":1739484076,\"endTime\":1739484088},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right, it can chat.\",\"startTime\":1739484082,\"endTime\":1739484084},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484085,\"endTime\":1739484086},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"bias. It''s there. It''s just built around, Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739484088,\"endTime\":1739484092},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, recognize it.\",\"startTime\":1739484092,\"endTime\":1739484094},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Read the scenario.\",\"startTime\":1739484098,\"endTime\":1739484099},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Teacher finds that chat cheapy tea.\",\"startTime\":1739484101,\"endTime\":1739484103},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Degenerated or that GPT generated content is biased? How should they address \",\"startTime\":1739484104,\"endTime\":1739484108},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"this with their students? \",\"startTime\":1739484108,\"endTime\":1739484111},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think first letting every student and user know that every GPT is biased. \",\"startTime\":1739484114,\"endTime\":1739484119},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I am biased meaning that it''s from my perspective, it''s from my construct, it''s from the way that my brain and my experiences have given me my my well of knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1739484119,\"endTime\":1739484129},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484124,\"endTime\":1739484124},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m culturally biased with what I have from my cultural inheritance and from experiences in life and the way that I learn even to express words and to even in the language that I have, it''s, it''s biasing me just that''s what it is. So. \",\"startTime\":1739484129,\"endTime\":1739484143},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484134,\"endTime\":1739484134},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Telling the students that everybody''s biased, GPTS are biased around their knowledge bases. And then second, you can help your GPT assistant or your GPT by giving \",\"startTime\":1739484144,\"endTime\":1739484153},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484150,\"endTime\":1739484151},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it knowledge based documents. Add this to the document. We want to include this, \",\"startTime\":1739484153,\"endTime\":1739484158},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and as you said, include this kind of author or include this type of person''s perspective. We want to make sure it''s well-rounded. \",\"startTime\":1739484158,\"endTime\":1739484167},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I was, I was seeing this maybe just a little bit different in terms of if I generated an assignment and I give it to the people in the class using ChatGPT or something like that. \",\"startTime\":1739484167,\"endTime\":1739484175},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Umm, but the content that I''ve shared with, with the kids is, is biased and maybe somebody points that out or whatever it is. And so how, how should you \",\"startTime\":1739484176,\"endTime\":1739484182},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"address that with the students? I mean, I think it''s a, you turn it into a learning \",\"startTime\":1739484182,\"endTime\":1739484186},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"situation. What we investigate what, what''s biased about it? What''s, what''s \",\"startTime\":1739484186,\"endTime\":1739484189},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"this, what''s that, you know? \",\"startTime\":1739484189,\"endTime\":1739484192},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How do you see that showing up? How do you think critically and analytically \",\"startTime\":1739484193,\"endTime\":1739484196},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"about this? What are the what are the structures that you''re gonna put in place \",\"startTime\":1739484196,\"endTime\":1739484199},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"as a as a learner or as a teacher to? \",\"startTime\":1739484199,\"endTime\":1739484202},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Ensure that you''re reducing as much bias as possible. How are you going to grow \",\"startTime\":1739484203,\"endTime\":1739484206},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"your lens around bias? Maybe you compare and contrast. Now you you generate \",\"startTime\":1739484206,\"endTime\":1739484210},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"another lesson. \",\"startTime\":1739484210,\"endTime\":1739484213},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That that says remove all bias of Indigenous languages, what I don''t know, whatever you know, and then do another one that has bias all through it. And so you''re \",\"startTime\":1739484213,\"endTime\":1739484222},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"growing that. So you''re comparing and contrasting growing the knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1739484222,\"endTime\":1739484226},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So kids are becoming more able to recognize that as the product is being being produced and and sent out to them. \",\"startTime\":1739484226,\"endTime\":1739484234},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So that was what I was just thinking about, about that learning, learning piece. \",\"startTime\":1739484236,\"endTime\":1739484240},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I really appreciate that you got that. Yeah, I think.\",\"startTime\":1739484236,\"endTime\":1739484238},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I appreciate you got that back to the student in the classroom and what that would look like in in engaging them in discourse around what do you think? What \",\"startTime\":1739484240,\"endTime\":1739484246},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and what could we do about this and where do you be the bias? Yeah, I really \",\"startTime\":1739484246,\"endTime\":1739484249},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"appreciate that. \",\"startTime\":1739484249,\"endTime\":1739484251},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484249,\"endTime\":1739484250},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Really. Tell me more. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484251,\"endTime\":1739484253},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thanks, Scott. Appreciate you.\",\"startTime\":1739484258,\"endTime\":1739484260},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''ll be right back. See you soon.\",\"startTime\":1739484261,\"endTime\":1739484263},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, I''ll see you in a second. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1739484262,\"endTime\":1739484263}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.394743+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.394743+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 896, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.186Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('9c50390f-c4ca-4e51-b328-15aceca7704c', 'd8e9db8f-f716-4f11-9fb9-c204d951fd7d', '134653', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So a current problem of practice or school improvement plan that we are working on is actually riding the school improvement plan. We just completed a strategic \",\"startTime\":1732055101,\"endTime\":1732055114},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"plan that ends in 20-30, so six years. And so we are aligning our. \",\"startTime\":1732055114,\"endTime\":1732055121},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"SIP plan, our school improvement plans with the strategic plan. So that''s kind \",\"startTime\":1732055122,\"endTime\":1732055126},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"of an area that we''re currently working on. And a problem of practice right \",\"startTime\":1732055126,\"endTime\":1732055130},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"now that I''m focused on is intervention in our building. \",\"startTime\":1732055130,\"endTime\":1732055134},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"What that looks like, how we operate, how to best fit intervention time and instead of doing pull out models, doing push insurance. So looking at data and \",\"startTime\":1732055134,\"endTime\":1732055141},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"analyzing that. \",\"startTime\":1732055141,\"endTime\":1732055145},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So to discuss the progress with my school improvement plan, we''re at the very beginning of the school improvement plan mostly because we have a new format. \",\"startTime\":1732055172,\"endTime\":1732055181},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"We worked on it as a district leadership team about a week ago. We have a meeting \",\"startTime\":1732055181,\"endTime\":1732055186},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"actually this week to discuss future ready and its ability to fit within our school improvement plan at the secondary level middle school. \",\"startTime\":1732055186,\"endTime\":1732055195},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So progress is at the beginning stages and hopefully have it written here shortly. \",\"startTime\":1732055195,\"endTime\":1732055201},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Challenges that I anticipate in the coming months, umm, include possibly, umm, staff being out due to illness, uh, and so having to cover staff absences. Umm, \",\"startTime\":1732055221,\"endTime\":1732055234},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"also just kind of that stretch of time where behaviors, uh, tend to increase, uh, as students look forward to breaks and how do we continue to. \",\"startTime\":1732055234,\"endTime\":1732055247},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Impress upon them the importance of causes of behavior.\",\"startTime\":1732055248,\"endTime\":1732055251},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Increasing our our incentives and rewards and making sure that students kind of finish strong as we move towards the end of the semester. \",\"startTime\":1732055251,\"endTime\":1732055261}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.097633+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.097633+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 131, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.036Z", "session_title": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1416", "name": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('b6ad603e-ab82-4da2-9df8-d6777e030c02', '4f2c17d9-95b8-4de7-8b97-ea6e0874f465', '134626', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11351\",\"text\":\"My name is A.J. Brown, Principal Sacagawea. Hoping to just connect with people \",\"startTime\":1732054516,\"endTime\":1732054520},{\"speaker\":\"11351\",\"text\":\"around the state. Other administrators pick their brains. \",\"startTime\":1732054520,\"endTime\":1732054524}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.267241+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.267241+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 15, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.202Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('85717ab3-a722-41b5-af04-0a2d0ccfbb57', 'd8e9db8f-f716-4f11-9fb9-c204d951fd7d', '134630', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Hi, my name is Katie Hamrick and I''m the principal at East Valley Middle School in Spokane, WA. I''m a first year principal and I hope to learn about a lot of \",\"startTime\":1732054600,\"endTime\":1732054610},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"things that will help me be successful, run a strong successful building, and work with amazing students and staff. \",\"startTime\":1732054610,\"endTime\":1732054620}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.460052+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.460052+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 25, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.255Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('08bf61ce-1e08-4beb-80cd-406a66ebd915', 'cd985910-e971-4907-988f-d311b2adb4d1', '110566', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:55.021299+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:55.021299+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 137, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:54.960Z", "session_title": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "197", "name": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('372c54a2-73e7-4b6f-9c3d-6c425c95799c', 'e5a67ee9-d30e-4f26-bafd-bf20b9ba4ab6', '138556', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Name is Michael and I hope to learn about.\",\"startTime\":1746632506,\"endTime\":1746632509},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Better ways to increase the to and through college rate across the state of Washington because I hear it''s struggling. \",\"startTime\":1746632509,\"endTime\":1746632515},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I know it''s important.\",\"startTime\":1746632516,\"endTime\":1746632517},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"And.\",\"startTime\":1746632518,\"endTime\":1746632519},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''m here to learn about how people are using.\",\"startTime\":1746632521,\"endTime\":1746632524},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Modern tools.\",\"startTime\":1746632525,\"endTime\":1746632526},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Encouraging the FAFSA, etc.\",\"startTime\":1746632528,\"endTime\":1746632530},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Aggressive, straight downhill, fast.\",\"startTime\":1746632548,\"endTime\":1746632550},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I tend to lead.\",\"startTime\":1746632553,\"endTime\":1746632554},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Through helping people do things that they think they''re scared of.\",\"startTime\":1746632557,\"endTime\":1746632561},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Kind of like a ski instructor would, or a whitewater kayaking instructor.\",\"startTime\":1746632563,\"endTime\":1746632568},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I think the people are very capable and.\",\"startTime\":1746632571,\"endTime\":1746632574},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Helping them understand how capable they are is really effective.\",\"startTime\":1746632574,\"endTime\":1746632577},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Hop like a Bunny everywhere I go. Just hippity hop, Hippity hippity hop, hop. \",\"startTime\":1746632595,\"endTime\":1746632598},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Hippity, hippity hop hop like a Bunny.\",\"startTime\":1746632598,\"endTime\":1746632600},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Not like a deer, not like a kangaroo. I like to hop like a Bunny. It''s so fun. \",\"startTime\":1746632602,\"endTime\":1746632605},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"At least track of time. I love to hop like a Bunny. \",\"startTime\":1746632605,\"endTime\":1746632609}]"', '2025-05-07 17:02:33.508682+00', '2025-05-07 17:02:33.508682+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 82, "created_at": "2025-05-07T17:02:33.313Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('e79dadb0-1b9d-4dd4-a507-b27db365350d', '8fb45423-222c-4ae3-b697-6e1187167e6e', '137047', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey, guys.\",\"startTime\":1739476252,\"endTime\":1739476252},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"This is Diego.\",\"startTime\":1739476252,\"endTime\":1739476253},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"About scientists, software developer and STEAM educator.\",\"startTime\":1739476254,\"endTime\":1739476259},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Nice to meet you all.\",\"startTime\":1739476259,\"endTime\":1739476260},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Here to give it a try and to collaborate.\",\"startTime\":1739476261,\"endTime\":1739476264},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Thank you very much.\",\"startTime\":1739476266,\"endTime\":1739476267},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey guys, this is Diego.\",\"startTime\":1739476288,\"endTime\":1739476290},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m a math scientist, software developer, STEAM educator and I love being here and can''t wait to meet you virtually. \",\"startTime\":1739476290,\"endTime\":1739476298},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Oh well, I believe in hands on.\",\"startTime\":1739476384,\"endTime\":1739476387},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Learning. I believe in science as a tool.\",\"startTime\":1739476387,\"endTime\":1739476390},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"To explore.\",\"startTime\":1739476392,\"endTime\":1739476393},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think that the role of the teacher is to facilitate processes. The role of \",\"startTime\":1739476394,\"endTime\":1739476399},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"the learner is to learn whatever they feel. \",\"startTime\":1739476399,\"endTime\":1739476403},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Emotionally connected to.\",\"startTime\":1739476405,\"endTime\":1739476407},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We we always learn what what we want to learn what you change, I think.\",\"startTime\":1739476409,\"endTime\":1739476414},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Indoor teaching.\",\"startTime\":1739476418,\"endTime\":1739476419},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Things we spent too much time inside and what you stay the same having groups of diverse students all together in. \",\"startTime\":1739476420,\"endTime\":1739476429},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Person in one place? Yeah, that''s it.\",\"startTime\":1739476432,\"endTime\":1739476436},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m thinking about kids.\",\"startTime\":1739476437,\"endTime\":1739476438},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey, so my stance about learning is that we learned first of all hands on something. \",\"startTime\":1739476458,\"endTime\":1739476465},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We learned through.\",\"startTime\":1739476465,\"endTime\":1739476466},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Uh, iterative process.\",\"startTime\":1739476468,\"endTime\":1739476469},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Where we go from an idea to something.\",\"startTime\":1739476470,\"endTime\":1739476473},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Concrete materialization.\",\"startTime\":1739476474,\"endTime\":1739476476},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"This realm.\",\"startTime\":1739476477,\"endTime\":1739476478},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We use science as an exploratory tool.\",\"startTime\":1739476480,\"endTime\":1739476483},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"What''s the role of the teacher is to facilitate the learning?\",\"startTime\":1739476485,\"endTime\":1739476488},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Learning is to actively pursue whatever they want to learn what you change. \",\"startTime\":1739476490,\"endTime\":1739476495},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think I''m thinking in terms of traditional learning. \",\"startTime\":1739476495,\"endTime\":1739476500},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"And I''m thinking about the school system in particular. I think we should.\",\"startTime\":1739476502,\"endTime\":1739476507},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Less time inside the classroom and what choose?\",\"startTime\":1739476510,\"endTime\":1739476514},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I mean, yeah, in in what you stay the same is that in person learning is.\",\"startTime\":1739476515,\"endTime\":1739476520},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Is better because we perceive other people''s vibes and we can resonate with them. Sometimes that''s a different. \",\"startTime\":1739476521,\"endTime\":1739476529},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"That''s a little different when we connect to virtually, but.\",\"startTime\":1739476530,\"endTime\":1739476533},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think uh.\",\"startTime\":1739476534,\"endTime\":1739476534},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I can I can perceive the vibes of somebody through.\",\"startTime\":1739476536,\"endTime\":1739476540},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Mediums like this so.\",\"startTime\":1739476541,\"endTime\":1739476542},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Oh well, what do they do for slow activity? I love training jujitsu.\",\"startTime\":1739476570,\"endTime\":1739476574},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m a round built. I''ve been training for almost 10 years. It helps me develop \",\"startTime\":1739476575,\"endTime\":1739476578},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"my creativity and my resilience. \",\"startTime\":1739476578,\"endTime\":1739476582},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"And when you''re slow rolling or rolling against another.\",\"startTime\":1739476584,\"endTime\":1739476587},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Person, sometimes you get into this flow mental state where your body moves. \",\"startTime\":1739476589,\"endTime\":1739476594},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Umm, myself.\",\"startTime\":1739476595,\"endTime\":1739476596},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I also love playing guitar, making music, I love improvising with other musicians. \",\"startTime\":1739476597,\"endTime\":1739476603},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"That''s really cool for me and.\",\"startTime\":1739476604,\"endTime\":1739476606},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Yeah, there''s two things I do for fun, Jiu jitsu and music.\",\"startTime\":1739476607,\"endTime\":1739476610}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880696+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880696+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 156, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.828Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c12da6aa-e9a3-4b94-a177-5398ba10818a', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135678', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"A. What are the chances?\",\"startTime\":1734048046,\"endTime\":1734048047},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, hey, I know that guy.\",\"startTime\":1734048047,\"endTime\":1734048049},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''m like, I know I get so excited when I know people that''s like, I''m not, I don''t know who I''m getting, but it''s just so fun. It''s like, we did this the \",\"startTime\":1734048050,\"endTime\":1734048055},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"other day. So, so. \",\"startTime\":1734048055,\"endTime\":1734048057},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, I like your e-mail that you you like talking to yourself.\",\"startTime\":1734048055,\"endTime\":1734048059},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, I might have lied a little bit, but it''s actually, it''s not bad. It feels \",\"startTime\":1734048062,\"endTime\":1734048065},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"strange at first and then you''re like, oh gosh, I should take this seriously. \",\"startTime\":1734048065,\"endTime\":1734048069},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm, mm-hmm. I know I was like one of one of the first ones that I did. I \",\"startTime\":1734048071,\"endTime\":1734048075},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048074,\"endTime\":1734048074},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"was like, oh, was that thorough enough? I don''t know if I like really expanded \",\"startTime\":1734048075,\"endTime\":1734048079},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on that answer enough or that it got enough of the words that I wanted it to get so. \",\"startTime\":1734048079,\"endTime\":1734048086},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, cool.\",\"startTime\":1734048087,\"endTime\":1734048088},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Absolutely love it. So yeah. Yeah. So let me see. Let''s press more. Icebreaker. \",\"startTime\":1734048088,\"endTime\":1734048091},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Fun fact, something involved in during a high school that helped pay that. Whatever. \",\"startTime\":1734048091,\"endTime\":1734048095},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Let''s go to the next question. That''s right. Yeah. No, no, you''re good. No, \",\"startTime\":1734048095,\"endTime\":1734048099},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, I''m sorry, yeah, I totally pressed the wrong OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048098,\"endTime\":1734048101},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"no, we''re good. We''re good. \",\"startTime\":1734048099,\"endTime\":1734048102},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048103,\"endTime\":1734048103},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So yeah, you''ve got question two there. Yeah, OK, gotcha. OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048107,\"endTime\":1734048114},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, and I should tell you, the last two times that I''ve done this, and \",\"startTime\":1734048110,\"endTime\":1734048113},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''ve only done it twice. The first time like I lost connection and it kicked \",\"startTime\":1734048113,\"endTime\":1734048117},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"me out of the conversation. And then the second time, like it kind of froze \",\"startTime\":1734048117,\"endTime\":1734048121},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on me. So like I''ve had two technical things. So hopefully that doesn''t happen, \",\"startTime\":1734048121,\"endTime\":1734048124},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"but. \",\"startTime\":1734048124,\"endTime\":1734048128},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, we''ll see. We''ll see. Yeah, Yeah. No worries. No worries.\",\"startTime\":1734048130,\"endTime\":1734048133},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, sure. So I still feel relatively new to high school, but I think some of \",\"startTime\":1734048133,\"endTime\":1734048138},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But, uh, so why don''t you answer this question and then I''ll tell you what what what we did or what I remember doing, Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734048135,\"endTime\":1734048141},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the things that we have in place is like the high school and beyond planned, which is that requirement that students are kind of thinking about. \",\"startTime\":1734048138,\"endTime\":1734048147},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"You know what, what they''re gonna pursue afterwards and then, you know, since I''ve been a student, they kinda have these different pathway options to graduation to really start students thinking about, you know, are they gonna go to a trade school afterwards? Are they thinking no school, like are they just gonna go \",\"startTime\":1734048153,\"endTime\":1734048171},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"into the workforce and you know, I mean, are they gonna pursue college or whatever military? So that''s part of it. You know, a lot of that''s in our counseling \",\"startTime\":1734048171,\"endTime\":1734048179},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048179,\"endTime\":1734048180},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"center. And then we also have just different. \",\"startTime\":1734048179,\"endTime\":1734048183},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Informational nights for families that want to learn more about the different plans kind of after senior year and options. And we start presenting those students \",\"startTime\":1734048184,\"endTime\":1734048194},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"junior years. So we call it a soon to be senior night and invite a lot of different \",\"startTime\":1734048194,\"endTime\":1734048198},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048197,\"endTime\":1734048198},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"resources from the community to come talk about everything from the FAFSA to, you know, military branches. \",\"startTime\":1734048198,\"endTime\":1734048208},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, so and then all of our people in the Career Center are available all day long and that we''re lucky to have them staffed as full time employees. \",\"startTime\":1734048209,\"endTime\":1734048219},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yes, Good, good. Well, this is what thanks for sharing all that helps \",\"startTime\":1734048209,\"endTime\":1734048214},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"me remember what what what I did with the help of a lot of other people. And \",\"startTime\":1734048214,\"endTime\":1734048218},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"it really started with the creation of, I''ll call them pathways that kids were interested in that that were based upon what would have been the previous high school and beyond plan. So with a student coming up from the from the middle \",\"startTime\":1734048218,\"endTime\":1734048231},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So.\",\"startTime\":1734048223,\"endTime\":1734048224},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"school was like. \",\"startTime\":1734048231,\"endTime\":1734048235},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Science. A technology track, A STEM track. We had we had created like 7 different \",\"startTime\":1734048249,\"endTime\":1734048251},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"pathways. \",\"startTime\":1734048251,\"endTime\":1734048254},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That already pre slugged a lot of classes that kids had to take that were required, but the pre slugging of coursework actually allowed them to meet every single cater requirement for a four year school if that''s what they wanted to do. The \",\"startTime\":1734048257,\"endTime\":1734048270},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1734048260,\"endTime\":1734048264},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"kids didn''t know that, the families didn''t know that, but we knew that because the goal was to leave is to have to allow the student to have as many opportunities possible on the other side. \",\"startTime\":1734048270,\"endTime\":1734048283},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That they could have. And so we had. They would literally, literally get sheets \",\"startTime\":1734048285,\"endTime\":1734048290},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1734048288,\"endTime\":1734048288},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of paper with courses already filled in over a four year plan. \",\"startTime\":1734048290,\"endTime\":1734048294},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And they''d have room for electives in their freshman year, sophomore year, junior year, senior year. And then after those will get filled out again. That would \",\"startTime\":1734048295,\"endTime\":1734048302},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"set them up as academic press. And we want to take challenging coursework. We \",\"startTime\":1734048302,\"endTime\":1734048306},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"would have one-on-one meetings with kids, call them down after all the schedules came in and said, you know what, your test, your assessments. Three years have \",\"startTime\":1734048306,\"endTime\":1734048314},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"shown that you can succeed at this level. So we''re going to move you to this \",\"startTime\":1734048314,\"endTime\":1734048317},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"dishonest course or this AP course. And they''re like, what? \",\"startTime\":1734048317,\"endTime\":1734048321},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And then we work in conjunction with the counseling center to make that happen. \",\"startTime\":1734048323,\"endTime\":1734048326},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And we did all the other things with FAFSA and, and and pieces like that and then our advisory program. \",\"startTime\":1734048326,\"endTime\":1734048331},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"From the freshman year through the senior year has really created and developed, particularly around the freshman year was was transition high school and study habits and all those kinds of fees. And sophomore year was was really diving \",\"startTime\":1734048333,\"endTime\":1734048344},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"into your what would be now the high school and beyond plan and figuring out next steps. And and then the junior year was like, OK, college applications. \",\"startTime\":1734048344,\"endTime\":1734048352},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What''s that look like fast that we had invited junior parents to come to fast tonight is to get an understanding and then that that''s and the military and we brought everybody in like follow people. \",\"startTime\":1734048352,\"endTime\":1734048363},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048355,\"endTime\":1734048355},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And that that senior year was you''re filling out application and doing resumes and I''ll discuss. But the basic underpin was that course work that that the \",\"startTime\":1734048364,\"endTime\":1734048371},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"kids didn''t even know we had kids like surprise. Well, I don''t know if I''ve \",\"startTime\":1734048371,\"endTime\":1734048374},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048372,\"endTime\":1734048372},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"taken, I don''t know if I''ve taken the right classes to go to four year school. \",\"startTime\":1734048374,\"endTime\":1734048377},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And that''s not the end all be all. But we looked at like all the community colleges \",\"startTime\":1734048377,\"endTime\":1734048380},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"around Spokane and every single one of them, the certification required like an Algebra 2 level of math. So we just required every kid to take Algebra 2. \",\"startTime\":1734048380,\"endTime\":1734048387},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"They didn''t know. They don''t know. You just tell them what to take and they \",\"startTime\":1734048387,\"endTime\":1734048390},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"take it. \",\"startTime\":1734048390,\"endTime\":1734048393},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right, right. Well, I will say it was really one of the things that''s really \",\"startTime\":1734048396,\"endTime\":1734048401},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So anyway, that''s.\",\"startTime\":1734048397,\"endTime\":1734048398},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"gained popularity in our school is the college and the high school classes so that they can get that that credit before they go. And so that''s been really \",\"startTime\":1734048401,\"endTime\":1734048410},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Yep, Yep.\",\"startTime\":1734048406,\"endTime\":1734048407},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"helpful for, you know, the students. And then eventually hopefully we have enough \",\"startTime\":1734048410,\"endTime\":1734048414},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"classes that it can relieve some financial burden from them too. So. \",\"startTime\":1734048414,\"endTime\":1734048418},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"One of the things Matt would like to pursue is like a dual credit kind of, you know, like, let''s see how we can get most of their prereqs done so that when they go to college, they really have to do the required, you know, other stuff. \",\"startTime\":1734048418,\"endTime\":1734048429},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048419,\"endTime\":1734048420},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734048429,\"endTime\":1734048433},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah, no. And you that''s come in since I''ve left high school, you \",\"startTime\":1734048434,\"endTime\":1734048438},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"know all those pieces and that''s been integrated in but anyway, so yeah, yeah, it''s cool. And a better two year, 4 year trades will tech school. And I mean \",\"startTime\":1734048438,\"endTime\":1734048445},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048440,\"endTime\":1734048442},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the basic piece is just a foundational of of educated foundation of education. \",\"startTime\":1734048445,\"endTime\":1734048449},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So you can succeed and can get through like that ERDC data we share share with you like, you know, 50% of the kids after eight years have some certification. \",\"startTime\":1734048449,\"endTime\":1734048457},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I mean that needs to change so. \",\"startTime\":1734048457,\"endTime\":1734048460},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048460,\"endTime\":1734048462},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, but cool, cool. And I appreciate you saying like, yeah, middle school \",\"startTime\":1734048462,\"endTime\":1734048465},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"to high school. I''m not sure yet, but I''ll figure it out. \",\"startTime\":1734048465,\"endTime\":1734048469},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048469,\"endTime\":1734048469},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s awesome, It''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1734048471,\"endTime\":1734048473},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, so you so my thing is like it''s like flashing on me. It''s kind of bugging \",\"startTime\":1734048473,\"endTime\":1734048476},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"out. So I can''t see what the question says and I bet you I won''t be able to \",\"startTime\":1734048476,\"endTime\":1734048479},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"move on after that. \",\"startTime\":1734048479,\"endTime\":1734048482},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, we''ll see, we''ll see. What challenges do you face in assisting your students \",\"startTime\":1734048484,\"endTime\":1734048489},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048485,\"endTime\":1734048486},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"with post secondary goals? What challenges do you face with assisting students \",\"startTime\":1734048489,\"endTime\":1734048494},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"in their post secondary goals? And I''ll, I''ll start while you think about it. \",\"startTime\":1734048494,\"endTime\":1734048499},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, oh, I would, I would say that it''s, it''s the lack of, even though you have college and career counselors, it''s really the lack of. \",\"startTime\":1734048499,\"endTime\":1734048508},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I feel like actually.\",\"startTime\":1734048499,\"endTime\":1734048500},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, go ahead.\",\"startTime\":1734048502,\"endTime\":1734048503},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Hand holding a bunch of different well it comes from two things. I would say \",\"startTime\":1734048515,\"endTime\":1734048517},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the systemic nature. \",\"startTime\":1734048517,\"endTime\":1734048520},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Not necessarily just resources and council, but it''s really a belief system and A and A and a systemic process that happens in the middle school that is, \",\"startTime\":1734048521,\"endTime\":1734048529},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is ongoing and, and has multiple touch points through the middle school years on going through the high school years where students are seeing what''s possible and seeing their potential. And it''s also engaging the parents in a much younger, \",\"startTime\":1734048529,\"endTime\":1734048542},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"younger piece. \",\"startTime\":1734048542,\"endTime\":1734048546},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"To dispel some of the myths around financial assistance, like everybody looks at sticker shock. \",\"startTime\":1734048547,\"endTime\":1734048552},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And, and the bottom line, and that''s not the reality. You know when, when I''ll \",\"startTime\":1734048554,\"endTime\":1734048559},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just use my two kids as an example, they both chose independent schools or private schools where we got an enormous amount of financial aid and they got Zippo at the state schools. We actually went to private schools at a less cost out \",\"startTime\":1734048559,\"endTime\":1734048573},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of pocket than the state schools that were only offering loan money. And, and \",\"startTime\":1734048573,\"endTime\":1734048578},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"people don''t understand that. So the messaging early on to do that for. \",\"startTime\":1734048578,\"endTime\":1734048583},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The fact that you can use FAFSA or the Washington State Financial Aid Grant to go to an apprenticeship school, people don''t know that either. So there''s \",\"startTime\":1734048586,\"endTime\":1734048594},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"some pieces that have to happen early on. Systemically, it doesn''t. It can''t \",\"startTime\":1734048594,\"endTime\":1734048597},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048596,\"endTime\":1734048597},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"start in 9th grade. So I would say that''s the biggest piece. It''s not. Yes, \",\"startTime\":1734048597,\"endTime\":1734048601},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"those resources are counselors inside Bing. And really it''s a systemic piece \",\"startTime\":1734048601,\"endTime\":1734048605},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of this has to dig into the beliefs and install some of the myths at a much, much, much, much, much, much earlier grade level than high school. \",\"startTime\":1734048605,\"endTime\":1734048612},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I, I completely agree with you. I think that also we see, you know, it''s \",\"startTime\":1734048615,\"endTime\":1734048619},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like last year was the first year I was on kind of the scholarship committee of distributing money back to students. And it was the same students that applied \",\"startTime\":1734048619,\"endTime\":1734048627},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for kind of all the scholarships. And it''s just, it''s a small amount of kids. \",\"startTime\":1734048627,\"endTime\":1734048632},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, yes.\",\"startTime\":1734048630,\"endTime\":1734048631},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Like we were able to give them all at least one of the scholarships, but it was just like, man, like we are missing huge amounts of kids on here. I thought \",\"startTime\":1734048632,\"endTime\":1734048640},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"it was going to be like hundreds and hundreds of kids that we were kind of. \",\"startTime\":1734048640,\"endTime\":1734048644},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048645,\"endTime\":1734048646},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Choosing from and it wasn''t it was kind of like we were looking at the same, you know, 40 kids and they had applied for all of them and it was like, OK, So what is like the best fit for this kid? And then and so it''s great that they \",\"startTime\":1734048647,\"endTime\":1734048659},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yes, right, right. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048657,\"endTime\":1734048661},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"all got something, but it really doesn''t feel like it''s like this competitive, you know, thing that that many kids know about. And then yeah, I I completely \",\"startTime\":1734048659,\"endTime\":1734048668},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"agree with you. I think that a lot of families in particular don''t really know \",\"startTime\":1734048668,\"endTime\":1734048672},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"what the options are to. \",\"startTime\":1734048672,\"endTime\":1734048677},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Their students and so they''re kind of learning at the same time that the kids are learning. You know, it could be junior or senior year. And it''s like, man, \",\"startTime\":1734048677,\"endTime\":1734048684},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048683,\"endTime\":1734048684},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you l