xt\":\"be like firm, but kind of you want to, if you want to describe that, just being very firm with with students, but also kind and loving because you confess the kid out. But then at the very end of the day, the last sentence you say is I \",\"startTime\":1733237645,\"endTime\":1733237656},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237650,\"endTime\":1733237650},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237650,\"endTime\":1733237651},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"love you. \",\"startTime\":1733237656,\"endTime\":1733237660},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I love you, you''re important. You just got to get rid of those behaviors, you \",\"startTime\":1733237661,\"endTime\":1733237665},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237662,\"endTime\":1733237663},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"know, so but it''s the same thing just and I, I think I create the same thing with staff is that I''m firm, but I care about you. I''ll learn about you. I''ll \",\"startTime\":1733237665,\"endTime\":1733237673},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237666,\"endTime\":1733237669},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"do you know, I''ll send you cards. I will do the happy card. I want you to feel \",\"startTime\":1733237673,\"endTime\":1733237677},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"appreciated just like kids. And again, that structure, like you were saying, \",\"startTime\":1733237677,\"endTime\":1733237681},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"is just modeling that, just being vulnerable and modeling that and showing people that it happens that. \",\"startTime\":1733237681,\"endTime\":1733237689},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"That just being that firm and kind, but being firm, you have to be firm. You \",\"startTime\":1733237692,\"endTime\":1733237694},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"can''t just be Willy nilly. \",\"startTime\":1733237694,\"endTime\":1733237696},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Umm, with kids or adults, you know, and just in that openness and honesty.\",\"startTime\":1733237698,\"endTime\":1733237705},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, exactly. And it, it reminds me of the quote by Brené Brown that you''ve \",\"startTime\":1733237705,\"endTime\":1733237709},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"probably heard Jack use a million times and myself as clear, as kind. And, and \",\"startTime\":1733237709,\"endTime\":1733237713},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"when you say firm, I conjure up that notion of, of being clear with the expectations \",\"startTime\":1733237713,\"endTime\":1733237717},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and guidelines and, and reinforcing those for students and for students and adults, because that''s the kind thing to do when we can remove confusion about how I have to act and behave and be with others. \",\"startTime\":1733237717,\"endTime\":1733237729},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237721,\"endTime\":1733237721},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237728,\"endTime\":1733237728},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s but it''s tough to do for a lot of people.\",\"startTime\":1733237731,\"endTime\":1733237733},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah, for some people, but yeah, it''s that. It''s just that they want to be. \",\"startTime\":1733237734,\"endTime\":1733237738},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1733237737,\"endTime\":1733237738},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''m sorry. We''re not friends here. I mean, we are, but we aren''t, you know, \",\"startTime\":1733237738,\"endTime\":1733237742},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"it''s just like your kids. I''m not your friend. I love you. I''m not your friend. \",\"startTime\":1733237742,\"endTime\":1733237746},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733237742,\"endTime\":1733237742},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"And we don''t have to get along, but we do have to show respect to each other. \",\"startTime\":1733237746,\"endTime\":1733237749},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237747,\"endTime\":1733237749},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So. Or be respectful. Be respectful. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237749,\"endTime\":1733237753},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I love it. Love it. Perfect, perfect. Let''s slide over to the next one here. \",\"startTime\":1733237752,\"endTime\":1733237758},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, spend 3 open-ended minutes with Brenda. Well, look at that. Isn''t that nice? \",\"startTime\":1733237758,\"endTime\":1733237764},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Alright, try not to lose you.\",\"startTime\":1733237761,\"endTime\":1733237762},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Isn''t that nice? So remind me, what Rd. are you going down right now? Like this \",\"startTime\":1733237764,\"endTime\":1733237770},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is our open-ended time? Yeah. Gotcha. Oh, gotcha. OK, OK. \",\"startTime\":1733237770,\"endTime\":1733237776},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I right now I''m going down 176. I actually went down the long way because there''s \",\"startTime\":1733237782,\"endTime\":1733237786},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"like four or five roads that I could go down to get to my my job. I was going \",\"startTime\":1733237786,\"endTime\":1733237791},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"all the way down towards Pacific so that I didn''t get cut off with the, the sometimes when I enter, my service is not really good around here. So, so I \",\"startTime\":1733237791,\"endTime\":1733237800},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"was trying to go down a road that I knew I would have service. \",\"startTime\":1733237800,\"endTime\":1733237804},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, good, good thinking as you as.\",\"startTime\":1733237803,\"endTime\":1733237807},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But.\",\"startTime\":1733237806,\"endTime\":1733237807},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"As you call out the road names, I''m, I''m remembering my days at at PLU and all around Parkland and Spanaway and all that stuff. And I''m like, Oh yeah, I think \",\"startTime\":1733237810,\"endTime\":1733237816},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But yeah, no, I just passed district office, so I''m going to go down B Street and get to my building, so. \",\"startTime\":1733237810,\"endTime\":1733237816},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I ran down that road a few times during wrestling season. I know I''ve gone down \",\"startTime\":1733237816,\"endTime\":1733237819},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"that road. So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237819,\"endTime\":1733237822},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Awesome.\",\"startTime\":1733237828,\"endTime\":1733237828},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Awesome. Well, we can go to the next there. And, and and I, I kid you not, Brenda, \",\"startTime\":1733237831,\"endTime\":1733237836},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"when when, when I saw when I saw the match with Brenda show up, I was like Brenda, Brenda, Brenda, Brenda. Oh, my gosh, it''s Brenda Thompson. I''m so happy. It''s \",\"startTime\":1733237836,\"endTime\":1733237848},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just put a big smile on my face this morning. So I appreciate you. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237848,\"endTime\":1733237854},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Well, you guys always, you guys always do that for me and I appreciate you guys. \",\"startTime\":1733237851,\"endTime\":1733237855},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So I was like going to the meetings or just talking to you guys or just listening to you guys. Sometimes. Sometimes I don''t talk and I try to give other people \",\"startTime\":1733237855,\"endTime\":1733237863},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237863,\"endTime\":1733237863},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"space, but some people like it''s quite OK. Let me go ahead and say something. \",\"startTime\":1733237863,\"endTime\":1733237867},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s perfect, It''s perfect. And I don''t know if we''ll see each other \",\"startTime\":1733237868,\"endTime\":1733237872},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"''cause we may not get connected again through this, but if, if or if we''re there. \",\"startTime\":1733237872,\"endTime\":1733237876},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But happy holidays to you and your family. Yeah, hopefully get get the kids \",\"startTime\":1733237876,\"endTime\":1733237880},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"all around again and, and get some smiles and some laughter. I know you''ll laugh, \",\"startTime\":1733237880,\"endTime\":1733237884},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"YouTube.\",\"startTime\":1733237882,\"endTime\":1733237882},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"there''s no question about that. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237884,\"endTime\":1733237888},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"That''s all we do, tell stories. Horror stories.\",\"startTime\":1733237890,\"endTime\":1733237892},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That''s a that''s a given. Oh, yeah. Well, I got a story for you. Let me let me \",\"startTime\":1733237893,\"endTime\":1733237896},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"one up that one, you know, so, you know, you know how that goes. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237896,\"endTime\":1733237899},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But it''s like we we compare education and military stories.\",\"startTime\":1733237900,\"endTime\":1733237903},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237904,\"endTime\":1733237905},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Because my dad was military, too. So my husband and my dad have those stories. \",\"startTime\":1733237906,\"endTime\":1733237910},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, was he OK? Oh wow. Yeah, cool.\",\"startTime\":1733237909,\"endTime\":1733237913},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"And then my mom works in Spanaway Lake High School as their program nurse and one of the special Ed programs. So she has stories. But you know, just, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237910,\"endTime\":1733237918},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So it''s always story, story, stories. \",\"startTime\":1733237918,\"endTime\":1733237922},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Always, always. Well, I don''t know about you, but I guarantee you this is the \",\"startTime\":1733237924,\"endTime\":1733237928},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"best 15 minutes of my day. So thank you. All right. OK. OK. Make it a great \",\"startTime\":1733237928,\"endTime\":1733237931},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I appreciate it. I mine too right now. We''ll have to see what I get with kiddos. \",\"startTime\":1733237930,\"endTime\":1733237934},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"day, Brenda. Thanks. Bye. \",\"startTime\":1733237931,\"endTime\":1733237935},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"YouTube Bye bye sweetie.\",\"startTime\":1733237938,\"endTime\":1733237939}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.405415+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.405415+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 718, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.190Z", "session_title": "#learning_to_human", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "33", "name": "#learning_to_human", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "Inclusion"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c6be590f-15e5-4f9c-8601-daf0f0333e7c', '903382e8-a889-4f58-85bc-6ec0178aa685', '134647', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I''m good. How are you?\",\"startTime\":1732054765,\"endTime\":1732054767},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Hey, how are you?\",\"startTime\":1732054766,\"endTime\":1732054767},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Good. I''m supposed to share a fun fact about myself. I grew up in New York City \",\"startTime\":1732054768,\"endTime\":1732054774},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"and my wife grew up in a town of 500 in rural Eastern Oregon. \",\"startTime\":1732054774,\"endTime\":1732054781},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1732054781,\"endTime\":1732054782},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I guess fun fact for me is I used to own a custom sugar cookie business. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1732054783,\"endTime\":1732054788},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What makes you an effective leader? That''s a leader. Well, that''s pretty cool. \",\"startTime\":1732054787,\"endTime\":1732054791},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"that''s pretty cool. \",\"startTime\":1732054788,\"endTime\":1732054793},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What caused you to pivot to education? \",\"startTime\":1732054791,\"endTime\":1732054795},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Well, I did it while I was in education. It was at the same time and I decided \",\"startTime\":1732054800,\"endTime\":1732054804},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"to end that because time. \",\"startTime\":1732054804,\"endTime\":1732054807},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054808,\"endTime\":1732054808},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"All right, what makes you an effective leader?\",\"startTime\":1732054811,\"endTime\":1732054814},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Umm.\",\"startTime\":1732054813,\"endTime\":1732054813},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''ve been told one of the reasons is I''m present and I''m willing to jump in and do anything and I lead by example. How about you? \",\"startTime\":1732054817,\"endTime\":1732054827},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Kind of similarly, I''ve been told that I am really present in buildings. I''m \",\"startTime\":1732054829,\"endTime\":1732054834},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"not somebody that''s usually like in my office a lot. I like to be in classrooms \",\"startTime\":1732054834,\"endTime\":1732054838},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"and out at recess. So I think just being around and listening to people would \",\"startTime\":1732054838,\"endTime\":1732054843},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"be a strength. \",\"startTime\":1732054843,\"endTime\":1732054847},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What''s the next? Yeah, my, my supervisors like your office. Looks like you barely \",\"startTime\":1732054847,\"endTime\":1732054850},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"moved in. I said. I have ''cause I don''t like spending time here. My my office \",\"startTime\":1732054850,\"endTime\":1732054853},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"is the school. And she goes, that''s perfect. \",\"startTime\":1732054853,\"endTime\":1732054857},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054858,\"endTime\":1732054859},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Next What''s your next goal in your leadership journey?\",\"startTime\":1732054865,\"endTime\":1732054868},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I would say that mine is. This is my fourth year in administration and 4th year \",\"startTime\":1732054869,\"endTime\":1732054875},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"as an API. Took a year off last year to go in the classroom and finish my dissertation \",\"startTime\":1732054875,\"endTime\":1732054880},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"and then I decided to go back into the AP role this year. But I would like to \",\"startTime\":1732054880,\"endTime\":1732054886},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"move into principle eventually. I just have two young children so I''m not. \",\"startTime\":1732054886,\"endTime\":1732054892},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"5:00 and 7:00.\",\"startTime\":1732054893,\"endTime\":1732054894},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah. How old are your kids? Nice. Yeah. We have an 11 year old who just started \",\"startTime\":1732054895,\"endTime\":1732054899},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"middle school, so I understand that part. Oh, yeah. You know, it''s a good question \",\"startTime\":1732054899,\"endTime\":1732054904},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"about my next goal and my leadership journey because I the previous 10 years I was a principal at self-contained behavior schools. \",\"startTime\":1732054904,\"endTime\":1732054913},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054904,\"endTime\":1732054905},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"The last seven in my current district and so.\",\"startTime\":1732054916,\"endTime\":1732054919},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m enjoying the transition to a comprehensive school, but there''s moments where \",\"startTime\":1732054921,\"endTime\":1732054925},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m like, you know, I think I could do this for maybe five years and then I may just leave education just because some days that the trends don''t seem as as wanting to do it for a while. But we''ve got folks at my district who think \",\"startTime\":1732054925,\"endTime\":1732054937},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"what I''m doing is, is pretty solid. And so I think I could grow in the district, \",\"startTime\":1732054937,\"endTime\":1732054941},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Absolutely.\",\"startTime\":1732054940,\"endTime\":1732054941},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"but I don''t think at this point I would want to leave a building, go to central office to do something like that. \",\"startTime\":1732054941,\"endTime\":1732054949},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Umm, to me the kid action is where it is. It''s more fun than the adult. Actually, \",\"startTime\":1732054950,\"endTime\":1732054954},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"the adults cause me way more stress than than than the kids. \",\"startTime\":1732054954,\"endTime\":1732054957},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK. Strength of our schools culture. I would say that we have very strong staff \",\"startTime\":1732054963,\"endTime\":1732054968},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"to staff relationships. \",\"startTime\":1732054968,\"endTime\":1732054972},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054974,\"endTime\":1732054974},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"It''s a community that really values community because it''s a small neighborhood school, so everyone kind of knows each other and their families and staff have been there for a really long time, so they know the families. There''s a really \",\"startTime\":1732054975,\"endTime\":1732054986},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"strong sense of community, especially among teachers and then like teachers to families. \",\"startTime\":1732054986,\"endTime\":1732054994},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054993,\"endTime\":1732054994},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yeah, we have a, we have a similar feeling. We''ve got, I''ve got two teachers \",\"startTime\":1732054996,\"endTime\":1732055001},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"who''ve been teaching in our building for 3132 years and teaching kindergarten the whole time. And like they kind of are like Mary Poppins personified. And \",\"startTime\":1732055001,\"endTime\":1732055010},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"we got some folks that are like kind of 2829, have a couple more years and then and then we''ve got other folks that are kind of new. But everyone is really \",\"startTime\":1732055010,\"endTime\":1732055019},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"proud that we work, that they work at our school. \",\"startTime\":1732055019,\"endTime\":1732055023},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You know that we work with our community and we''re champions and advocates for for that. So I think there''s a lot of. \",\"startTime\":1732055024,\"endTime\":1732055029},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Lot of lot of love strengthen that identity. It doesn''t always translate into \",\"startTime\":1732055030,\"endTime\":1732055034},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"then like putting in the effort for that identity ''cause we have a lot of folks who, you know, when at the moment the, the clock hits the end of contract time, they''re walking out the door and, and then they''re like, so you guys fix everything and we''ll be back tomorrow. It''s like, well, it doesn''t quite always work that \",\"startTime\":1732055034,\"endTime\":1732055051},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055048,\"endTime\":1732055048},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"way. So one of one of my goals with RAP is, is how do we keep shifting that \",\"startTime\":1732055051,\"endTime\":1732055056},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"to make it to get. \",\"startTime\":1732055056,\"endTime\":1732055060},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"More ownership. And it''s hard because the previous principal just kind of was \",\"startTime\":1732055061,\"endTime\":1732055065},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"fairly checked out and let people kind of do whatever they want. So kind of \",\"startTime\":1732055065,\"endTime\":1732055070},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"getting, getting back in trenches going to take a little bit of time. So let''s \",\"startTime\":1732055070,\"endTime\":1732055074},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"see where it goes. Yeah, sure. Yeah. There''ve been a couple days and, you know, \",\"startTime\":1732055074,\"endTime\":1732055078},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, OK. Yeah, I I would say yeah, we''re we''re pretty similar in that like \",\"startTime\":1732055074,\"endTime\":1732055078},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m, I''m still building, you know, relationships with, you know, everyone in the school. But there''s been moments where I kind of wanted to say, so you say \",\"startTime\":1732055078,\"endTime\":1732055087},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"idea of here you handle it, I''m clocked out type of thing, which I mean I get for. \",\"startTime\":1732055078,\"endTime\":1732055086},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"you''re all about kids. \",\"startTime\":1732055087,\"endTime\":1732055091},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"CBA and personal like mental health, but I would you know, love to see a little bit more. \",\"startTime\":1732055088,\"endTime\":1732055094},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Of that investment.\",\"startTime\":1732055096,\"endTime\":1732055098},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You say you''re all about our kids, but I don''t see it in your actions and help. \",\"startTime\":1732055110,\"endTime\":1732055113},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Can you help me understand the disconnect, but I don''t think that will help the relationship building and the work quite yet to say that, but it''s I think it a lot so. \",\"startTime\":1732055113,\"endTime\":1732055123},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, absolutely. OK.\",\"startTime\":1732055123,\"endTime\":1732055126},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK. Feel like we kind of already transitioned to this one a little bit, but \",\"startTime\":1732055130,\"endTime\":1732055137},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055134,\"endTime\":1732055137},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I do also think that we have a pretty general mistrust among staff towards admin. \",\"startTime\":1732055137,\"endTime\":1732055143},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"The the kind of like impression the last couple of years has been that they just stay in their office. So trying to break that narrative. I''ve gotten good \",\"startTime\":1732055144,\"endTime\":1732055153},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055152,\"endTime\":1732055153},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"feedback on it so far, so that''s good. \",\"startTime\":1732055153,\"endTime\":1732055158},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"But I think in general, like the relationship between staff and admin, and then we''re still working really hard on student to student relationships too. I think \",\"startTime\":1732055160,\"endTime\":1732055170},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"conflict resolution is not always a strength for us. \",\"startTime\":1732055170,\"endTime\":1732055175},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055170,\"endTime\":1732055170},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"No, no, I, I I see similar stuff.\",\"startTime\":1732055175,\"endTime\":1732055177},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You know, in our building as you know, the work in, in regards to, you know, kind of where we''re going. It was interesting. I had a thought it had vanished \",\"startTime\":1732055180,\"endTime\":1732055188},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"and it''ll come back in a minute. But you know, this is, is one of the things \",\"startTime\":1732055188,\"endTime\":1732055192},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"that I walked into. \",\"startTime\":1732055192,\"endTime\":1732055196},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Which kind of speaks to my strengths is the person before me was in their office a lot. And so we had a couple first grade teachers who told me like the second \",\"startTime\":1732055199,\"endTime\":1732055208},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"week, I''ve seen you more in my classroom already than I saw the entire principle the previous year. And so to me, that was a comment that we''re doing the right \",\"startTime\":1732055208,\"endTime\":1732055216},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"thing. And you know, when we had some issues in fifth grade at like lunch and \",\"startTime\":1732055216,\"endTime\":1732055220},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055216,\"endTime\":1732055217},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"recess, you know, my AP and I were, you know, we''re like, OK, so we will be at every recess and every lunch is being visible and just being visible. \",\"startTime\":1732055220,\"endTime\":1732055228},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Coming up to us, helping us, you know, asking us to help solve the problem. \",\"startTime\":1732055228,\"endTime\":1732055232},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"So it''s like that visibility piece is so key. And I think, you know, that''s \",\"startTime\":1732055232,\"endTime\":1732055236},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"how we change that culture is by having our teachers see us solving the problems \",\"startTime\":1732055236,\"endTime\":1732055240},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"that we''re communicating with them about the problems that we''re solving and bringing them into the problem solving process so that they have more tools and capacity. And really trying to be like, I will cover your classroom while \",\"startTime\":1732055240,\"endTime\":1732055251},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"you step out and have that conversation with the student rather than me have that conversation with the student be that''s going to. \",\"startTime\":1732055251,\"endTime\":1732055258},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And it''s going to keep their power. But some of our teachers don''t want the \",\"startTime\":1732055258,\"endTime\":1732055263},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"power. They want us just to solve it and the kids to listen to them. And it \",\"startTime\":1732055263,\"endTime\":1732055267},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"doesn''t really work these days like that. So. Right. Yeah. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1732055267,\"endTime\":1732055271},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, more, more the compliance piece, right. Just just get him to do it. Whatever, \",\"startTime\":1732055268,\"endTime\":1732055271},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1732055271,\"endTime\":1732055274},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Well, thank you.\",\"startTime\":1732055280,\"endTime\":1732055280},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055282,\"endTime\":1732055283},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I, well, this kind of doesn''t really count. This was a great conversation too, \",\"startTime\":1732055284,\"endTime\":1732055287},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"but I really enjoyed our conversation around discipline earlier today and like the resources you shared. So like, that''s the first thing that popped into my \",\"startTime\":1732055287,\"endTime\":1732055292},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"mind. \",\"startTime\":1732055292,\"endTime\":1732055295},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Oh, awesome. Cool. Well, I appreciate our chat both earlier and now. What I \",\"startTime\":1732055296,\"endTime\":1732055300},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"think is always good about these connections is that doesn''t matter what part of the state that we''re in, some of the challenges we''re dealing with are identical. \",\"startTime\":1732055300,\"endTime\":1732055309},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And you know, so it doesn''t, it doesn''t matter if we''re in Vancouver or Seattle, Spokane or anywhere in between, which helped remind me last week since I''ve had a couple teachers taking some like kind of personal digs. \",\"startTime\":1732055309,\"endTime\":1732055322},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And I remind I had to like with the conversation with my AP kind of pulled me out of they''re angry at the principal position. They''re not angry at me personally. \",\"startTime\":1732055323,\"endTime\":1732055332},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And so that that part is helpful. And I think these conversations and the connections \",\"startTime\":1732055332,\"endTime\":1732055336},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"really help in that. Like it''s a, you know, the anger is not at us personal. \",\"startTime\":1732055336,\"endTime\":1732055340},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"It just feels personal because we have so much investment in what we''re doing. \",\"startTime\":1732055340,\"endTime\":1732055345},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And so it''s, you know, kind of that professional personal balance of kind of investing, but not to the point where we''re taking the feedback personally. \",\"startTime\":1732055345,\"endTime\":1732055353},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I love that. That''s good. That''s a nice little nugget.\",\"startTime\":1732055356,\"endTime\":1732055358}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.45409+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.45409+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 605, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.374Z", "session_title": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1416", "name": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('87fa442c-5a23-4806-ba99-6fba0e12533c', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '86134', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.104347+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.104347+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 183, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:27.041Z", "session_title": "Preparing for Committee Leads Meeting - Action Plan", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "336", "name": "Preparing for Committee Leads Meeting - Action Plan", "tags": [{"name": "Pathfinder"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fc7f9032-8cbf-4edf-8eab-73d86138bced', '72c8622a-73ad-405b-9f71-d437a1193d3d', '74392', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.985288+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.985288+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 694, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.927Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fcf4e9d6-09cc-4a06-b742-bc22ea99d0b3', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '78021', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.118937+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.118937+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 429, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.907Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('37e69fdd-9e3c-4e32-b5cc-8544b1960af6', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '136250', '"[{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"This prompter is about what are the real and misplaced fears that educators might have when using AI tools in education. \",\"startTime\":1736971759,\"endTime\":1736971765},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"The real fears are, I think around the world atrophy that like if you don''t use it, you lose it. And so they start to lean on these tools to do parts of \",\"startTime\":1736971767,\"endTime\":1736971775},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"our life for us. Will we still be able to? What will we lose? \",\"startTime\":1736971775,\"endTime\":1736971780},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"A self driving car is a good that kind of physical analogy of this in that like if a kid never learns how to drive, a kid couldn''t drive. Like the fact that \",\"startTime\":1736971783,\"endTime\":1736971791},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"us adults have been driving for 10/20/30 years. \",\"startTime\":1736971791,\"endTime\":1736971796},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Means like for example we can drive in the snow or when the conditions are bad. \",\"startTime\":1736971798,\"endTime\":1736971801},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So when needed to drive, we can drive where if you were never, never needed to drive, you would never become a competent driver. I''m sure there are other \",\"startTime\":1736971804,\"endTime\":1736971813},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"examples of that in the rest of the things that we do like writing, choosing words, calculating. So. So that''s a real fear. \",\"startTime\":1736971813,\"endTime\":1736971822},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I think the misplaced fear is that we''ll end up somewhere worse because of that, because. \",\"startTime\":1736971829,\"endTime\":1736971834},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"From my perspective, we''ve been.\",\"startTime\":1736971836,\"endTime\":1736971839},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We''ve been doing things differently for our entire like, history of the people. \",\"startTime\":1736971843,\"endTime\":1736971848},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Is the story I like to tell about when like that the Donner party had to eat each other when walking over Donner Pass and now I can drive up and over twice a week I during snowstorms, etcetera, because we''ve invented the snow plow and we''ve invented the automobile and we''ve paved roads. Like there are things that \",\"startTime\":1736971851,\"endTime\":1736971870},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I don''t need to know how to do, I don''t get to know how to do. \",\"startTime\":1736971870,\"endTime\":1736971875},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"But it''s kind of made life bigger and better.\",\"startTime\":1736971880,\"endTime\":1736971884},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So when we talk about bias in AI models.\",\"startTime\":1736971921,\"endTime\":1736971925},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We get to explore bias against the status quo, like is it less biased or more biased in our current systems? And, and it''s so good that we''re aware of this. \",\"startTime\":1736971927,\"endTime\":1736971939},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So for example, we know that AI is trained on existing writing things that have already been written down or pictures that have already been posted. \",\"startTime\":1736971939,\"endTime\":1736971950},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So it''s like our our lives until this point become like bait in and that we have historically had bias. So and that the people who''ve had more voice, for \",\"startTime\":1736971955,\"endTime\":1736971965},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"example, are the are people who are in power. They say history was written by \",\"startTime\":1736971965,\"endTime\":1736971969},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"the winners. And so the like the intelligence is trained in our our culture, \",\"startTime\":1736971969,\"endTime\":1736971974},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"but our written culture, as we go into video and image, it becomes into the culture of the. \",\"startTime\":1736971974,\"endTime\":1736971983},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Cruise groups of people who''ve been able to speak in that language, in the language of video and the language of of imagery. So it''s not everybody. \",\"startTime\":1736971987,\"endTime\":1736971992},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We''re not, it''s not it''s really not everybody''s voice or everybody''s perspective. \",\"startTime\":1736971994,\"endTime\":1736971998},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Umm, but it''s measurable and correctable at the system level instead of the individual level. So for that reason, it''s maybe probably better than the status \",\"startTime\":1736971998,\"endTime\":1736972007},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"quo. And I guess that''s a through line in both of both of these cards for me \",\"startTime\":1736972007,\"endTime\":1736972012},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"so far is that it seems of course, this is true, but it''s better. But but with \",\"startTime\":1736972012,\"endTime\":1736972016},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"it is better than without. So let''s keep going. \",\"startTime\":1736972016,\"endTime\":1736972021},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"There are large organizations working on bias correcting and.\",\"startTime\":1736972027,\"endTime\":1736972031},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And getting it right is properly incentivized. So. So I''m faithful that we as \",\"startTime\":1736972033,\"endTime\":1736972036},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"humanity will get that part right. \",\"startTime\":1736972036,\"endTime\":1736972040},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"In the offering of opportunity, there''s this like if you take the idea of AI was gonna decide who gets a loan and who does not. And it looks like who has \",\"startTime\":1736972043,\"endTime\":1736972051},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"historically given a loan, who historically is not. And we''re getting different \",\"startTime\":1736972051,\"endTime\":1736972055},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"opportunities to different people based on based on this bias. \",\"startTime\":1736972055,\"endTime\":1736972059},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"It''s a fun question. So it''s flipping now instead of a learner or a user, I''m \",\"startTime\":1736972087,\"endTime\":1736972091},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I''m engaged as a teacher. So if I''m demonstrating the impact of artificial intelligence \",\"startTime\":1736972091,\"endTime\":1736972096},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"and there''s bias and I''m showing that to learners and it''s their first time encountering these systems, the work would be to acknowledge it. Make sure that \",\"startTime\":1736972096,\"endTime\":1736972104},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"for generations we don''t forget to check our bias, especially at the system level. So acknowledge it, teach it, and trust. \",\"startTime\":1736972104,\"endTime\":1736972113},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"That over generations will get better and better.\",\"startTime\":1736972113,\"endTime\":1736972115}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.913934+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.913934+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 334, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.845Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fe48ea0d-b969-4e68-a404-cbdafd94a813', '4c3a7dc1-10fb-45d6-a20e-f89f0e73af73', '135679', '"[{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Hi, this is Allison Larson. I''m doing a reflective session. How can schools \",\"startTime\":1734048171,\"endTime\":1734048176},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"bridge the knowledge gap for families unfamiliar with the high school to college and trade pipeline? We do a lot of trying to do family engagement activities. \",\"startTime\":1734048176,\"endTime\":1734048186},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We do. \",\"startTime\":1734048186,\"endTime\":1734048191},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Zoom sessions and also in person sessions for families. We are trying to engage \",\"startTime\":1734048192,\"endTime\":1734048196},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"our natural leaders group to be more knowledgeable because Edmonds the way we have. \",\"startTime\":1734048196,\"endTime\":1734048205},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Families who did not grow up in the United States, and so their understanding of schooling is completely different, and we have some cultural differences that we need to bridge. So we tried to find a variety of ways to provide resources, \",\"startTime\":1734048205,\"endTime\":1734048222},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"and we''re always looking for more opportunities to engage families further. \",\"startTime\":1734048222,\"endTime\":1734048227},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We try to do things.\",\"startTime\":1734048229,\"endTime\":1734048230},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Multiple times during the school year and try to provide information in a bunch of different ways for families. \",\"startTime\":1734048232,\"endTime\":1734048238},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Card talks about umm, what we can do more specifically for families and provides. \",\"startTime\":1734048297,\"endTime\":1734048304},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Some good suggestions like parent teacher meetings about explaining post secondary options. \",\"startTime\":1734048304,\"endTime\":1734048310},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Umm, we do we? I haven''t thought of that, so that might be a really interesting. \",\"startTime\":1734048311,\"endTime\":1734048316},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Strategy for parents. We do do a lot of workshops about financial planning. \",\"startTime\":1734048317,\"endTime\":1734048322},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"This year we are partnering with some community partners to come in and help families with filling out FAFSA and WAFSA, and we have some we partnered with some community organizations as well as just volunteers that can help families navigate through that process for financial planning. \",\"startTime\":1734048322,\"endTime\":1734048343},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And then of course, we also have a college and Career Center specialist who helps and answer those kinds of questions. \",\"startTime\":1734048344,\"endTime\":1734048351},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And I had not thought of creating a mentorship program connecting our parents and alumni. And that is a really interesting idea. And one thing that our parent \",\"startTime\":1734048353,\"endTime\":1734048365},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"group is wanting to do is establish an alumni organization for our school. So \",\"startTime\":1734048365,\"endTime\":1734048372},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"that would be interesting then to help create partnerships among that alumni. \",\"startTime\":1734048372,\"endTime\":1734048378},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"So in this question about parents feeling really overwhelmed by all the post secondary options and the financial aid. I think one thing that we are really \",\"startTime\":1734048442,\"endTime\":1734048454},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"trying to do in our school and trying to Foster and grow a natural leaders program where we are helping families that did not grow up in the United States and families of our multilingual students to connect with each other and then hopefully. \",\"startTime\":1734048454,\"endTime\":1734048471},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"They learn information that then they can pass along and connect to their cultural groups. And we do talk about in those meetings what are the ways students can \",\"startTime\":1734048471,\"endTime\":1734048480},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"graduate from high school and then also what are the post secondary options, I think sometimes. \",\"startTime\":1734048480,\"endTime\":1734048489},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We approach our families of multilingual students from a deficit lens and I think we sometimes forget that those families have some pretty big goals for their students to achieve and want to see their students do well and so. \",\"startTime\":1734048491,\"endTime\":1734048507},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"It I think it''s really important that we try to do that outreach. Of course \",\"startTime\":1734048509,\"endTime\":1734048514},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"we do have resources where we have a counselor for our multilingual program and we have two pair educators that support that program along with our teachers \",\"startTime\":1734048514,\"endTime\":1734048523},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"and the counselor and the para educators and our family resource advocate meet regularly to, to reach out to family specifically and build relationships with them. \",\"startTime\":1734048523,\"endTime\":1734048537},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And then invite them into the school so that we can have meetings and have those conversations with them. So it''s not a huge program yet, but the people who \",\"startTime\":1734048537,\"endTime\":1734048547},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"are participating in the program do so regularly because I think they''re finding connections at the school. So it''s exciting and I think it''s just going to take \",\"startTime\":1734048547,\"endTime\":1734048557},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"a few years to really get it going. But we really. \",\"startTime\":1734048557,\"endTime\":1734048562},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Appreciate those efforts for our Natural leaders families to learn more about post secondary options. \",\"startTime\":1734048564,\"endTime\":1734048570}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.269408+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.269408+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 323, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.997Z", "session_title": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1428", "name": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('913d471f-73b4-4adc-aaed-3d2d37250565', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '132332', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.465465+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.465465+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 303, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.388Z", "session_title": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "250", "name": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "tags": [{"name": "Cothinking Classrooms"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c348ff40-0044-4a02-a697-253331585914', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135458', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, let''s see what is what is GPT and what is their main function? GPT is a \",\"startTime\":1733238167,\"endTime\":1733238170},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"generative. \",\"startTime\":1733238170,\"endTime\":1733238173},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Pre trained something with text training stuff and it''s really for just understanding human generated messages and and information to make life a little bit simpler and easier for you in many different ways. \",\"startTime\":1733238174,\"endTime\":1733238189},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"GPT is a generative.\",\"startTime\":1733238212,\"endTime\":1733238214},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Pre trained text analyzer.\",\"startTime\":1733238215,\"endTime\":1733238217},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And the main functions are really just analyzing massive amounts of information and and answering questions and. \",\"startTime\":1733238220,\"endTime\":1733238225},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Providing information to you in a in a fashion that makes sense for you, and distilling of information to make things easier. \",\"startTime\":1733238227,\"endTime\":1733238236},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I should probably begin a new engagement with an AI versus remaining the same one. You''re not getting the information that you''re you''re looking for or you \",\"startTime\":1733238274,\"endTime\":1733238280},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"need to tweak something up. \",\"startTime\":1733238280,\"endTime\":1733238284},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think we, we, we look at human inquiry as the generator of the idea that we want to try and solve, we''re trying to work with and as we, as we do that human inquiry, then we utilize AI to make that happen with our prompt. And then we \",\"startTime\":1733238286,\"endTime\":1733238299},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"have to engage with that to make sure that it''s what we''re looking for. \",\"startTime\":1733238299,\"endTime\":1733238303},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"If it''s not what we''re looking for, then we might have to begin a new engagement or tweak the current engagement that we''re in. It''s really about being clear \",\"startTime\":1733238304,\"endTime\":1733238312},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"in terms of what you''re you''re looking for. But if we want to maintain continuity \",\"startTime\":1733238312,\"endTime\":1733238316},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and an understanding of the same conversation, then we''re going to we''re going to continue that unless something on the outside or something changes that we need to address in a different manner or different fashion. \",\"startTime\":1733238316,\"endTime\":1733238328},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"In terms of utilizing AI, it was really about.\",\"startTime\":1733238355,\"endTime\":1733238357},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Just attaching documents and, and diving deep into them and creating action plans as a result of school improvement plans and goals that people want to accomplish as I''ve worked with with staff. The other thing is utilizing that \",\"startTime\":1733238362,\"endTime\":1733238374},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"to utilizing AI to write observation reports and other stuff. What I''d really \",\"startTime\":1733238374,\"endTime\":1733238379},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"like to do is better understand how to utilize it with data and how to crunch data and, and, and turn things out. \",\"startTime\":1733238379,\"endTime\":1733238387}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.284497+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.284497+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 155, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.075Z", "session_title": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "197", "name": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('651c13b1-c874-4247-a428-17f050858843', '31f25266-25f6-40c6-b809-30b6e6bc2301', '135553', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Hello.\",\"startTime\":1733443371,\"endTime\":1733443371},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Shoot my.\",\"startTime\":1733443374,\"endTime\":1733443376},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I can hear you. Can you hear me? OK, Perfect.\",\"startTime\":1733443377,\"endTime\":1733443380},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Can you hear me OK?\",\"startTime\":1733443378,\"endTime\":1733443379},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443380,\"endTime\":1733443380},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, oh gosh, a new platform I don''t know how to use.\",\"startTime\":1733443382,\"endTime\":1733443385},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. This is my I mean, were you doing it the bell? Did you practice at bell \",\"startTime\":1733443387,\"endTime\":1733443390},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"to do it? \",\"startTime\":1733443390,\"endTime\":1733443392},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"No, I actually, I this is my first time like on here. I did like the couple \",\"startTime\":1733443393,\"endTime\":1733443398},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of ones you do by yourself. So yeah, I''ve never done this before. \",\"startTime\":1733443398,\"endTime\":1733443402},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, Oh my gosh. OK. And it says I''m not supposed to drive, but I was gonna, \",\"startTime\":1733443402,\"endTime\":1733443406},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I was gonna drive home and then do it at the same time. How do you feel about \",\"startTime\":1733443406,\"endTime\":1733443410},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that? I''m OK with it. You might have to read the questions, though, if that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443410,\"endTime\":1733443414},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, if you feel OK about it, I''m fine with it.\",\"startTime\":1733443412,\"endTime\":1733443415},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. OK, awesome. \",\"startTime\":1733443414,\"endTime\":1733443418},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, absolutely Fine. So my name is Mallory Wilson. I''m an assistant principal \",\"startTime\":1733443419,\"endTime\":1733443425},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"at Olympia High School, and this is my second year here. Oh, cool. \",\"startTime\":1733443425,\"endTime\":1733443430},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I''m Annie Parker. I am a principal in Renton School District. This is also my \",\"startTime\":1733443431,\"endTime\":1733443433},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"second year at my school. Before that I was an AP for five years in Seattle \",\"startTime\":1733443433,\"endTime\":1733443436},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"School District. \",\"startTime\":1733443436,\"endTime\":1733443439},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, nice. What school in Seattle? Oh, OK. I''m like, not from Seattle, but I \",\"startTime\":1733443439,\"endTime\":1733443443},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, gosh. I did two years at Salmon Bay K and then three years at Nova High \",\"startTime\":1733443441,\"endTime\":1733443446},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"lived there for a number of years and worked so like, I was a teacher there and everything. So yeah, that''s why I was wondering, but OK. \",\"startTime\":1733443443,\"endTime\":1733443452},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"School. Yeah. Where did you teach? In Seattle. Oh, wow. Yeah, I know. Right \",\"startTime\":1733443446,\"endTime\":1733443452},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"there. Yeah, absolutely. That little old facility. Wow. \",\"startTime\":1733443452,\"endTime\":1733443457},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So I taught at a residential treatment facility, but it was served by Seattle Public Schools, and it''s called Ryder, which is up in like Lake City Way. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733443459,\"endTime\":1733443469},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"yeah, Yep, exactly. So I worked at the school on that site. \",\"startTime\":1733443469,\"endTime\":1733443474},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And we only like taught the students that lived there. Yeah, exactly. OK, well, \",\"startTime\":1733443478,\"endTime\":1733443483},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I kind of remember that program, like it was kind of an inclusive, like \",\"startTime\":1733443483,\"endTime\":1733443486},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"let me I just click ahead to the next card then. OK. OK. So discuss the benefits \",\"startTime\":1733443483,\"endTime\":1733443489},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"you would go and that''s where you were. Yeah, Yeah, OK. Yep, just hit next and \",\"startTime\":1733443486,\"endTime\":1733443490},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of Co teaching for inclusion. Would you like to go first? \",\"startTime\":1733443489,\"endTime\":1733443494},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"then it''s going to do a yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443490,\"endTime\":1733443494},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Discuss the benefits of Co teaching for inclusion. Well, I mean, I think something \",\"startTime\":1733443505,\"endTime\":1733443510},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that is really unfortunate at the elementary level, it''s much trickier to Co teach. And I remember when I worked at Nova, there were millions of opportunities. \",\"startTime\":1733443510,\"endTime\":1733443521},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"That our paras would Co teach, our speed teachers would Co teach and they would just build the curriculum together around that. It''s it''s quite different in \",\"startTime\":1733443526,\"endTime\":1733443533},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"elementary where there''s a lot of pull out for special education. There are \",\"startTime\":1733443533,\"endTime\":1733443537},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"push in models that often times it''s like 20-30 minute quick hits and then, you know, it''s not really that coaching style. But I do think there''s a huge \",\"startTime\":1733443537,\"endTime\":1733443545},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"benefit if, if it''s doable, can we talk great results when special education teachers and Jenna teachers work together to go teach kids. And then it was \",\"startTime\":1733443545,\"endTime\":1733443552},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443545,\"endTime\":1733443546},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"really seamless. \",\"startTime\":1733443552,\"endTime\":1733443556},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Going into the lessons and differentiating the lessons and then also like meeting with all the learners at the same time. Yeah. What about you? Yeah, yeah, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443558,\"endTime\":1733443566},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So this is actually a great discussion prompt. We didn''t have many classes that \",\"startTime\":1733443566,\"endTime\":1733443572},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"were Co taught last year and we definitely saw a need for it this year and so. \",\"startTime\":1733443572,\"endTime\":1733443577},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We started kind of with the willing. I think that there was definitely willingness \",\"startTime\":1733443578,\"endTime\":1733443583},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"from our special Ed teachers to Co teach, but just there wasn''t enough training. \",\"startTime\":1733443583,\"endTime\":1733443588},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And so we partnered with C home and did some like intensive targeted training around a Co Top Model. And we''ve been really trying to mirror what what they''ve \",\"startTime\":1733443588,\"endTime\":1733443598},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"been doing for the past few years and so. \",\"startTime\":1733443598,\"endTime\":1733443602},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We''re seeing huge benefits to it. I would say that like just selfishly, like \",\"startTime\":1733443603,\"endTime\":1733443607},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the morale with staff is better and there''s like just trust being built there that these are our kids like. \",\"startTime\":1733443607,\"endTime\":1733443614},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, maybe I''m not the expert in math, but I am an expert in special education, you know, or that vice versa. But our students have no idea which ones are served \",\"startTime\":1733443615,\"endTime\":1733443624},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"in special education in those spaces. Ones aren''t. And I think our parents are \",\"startTime\":1733443624,\"endTime\":1733443628},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"definitely like, please tell me there''s going to be a Co taught math next year for my kid. You know, please tell me there''s going to be a Co taught English. \",\"startTime\":1733443628,\"endTime\":1733443636},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And so we''re seeing some really huge successes and. \",\"startTime\":1733443636,\"endTime\":1733443641},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I think our teachers are just kind of pleasantly surprised by it so.\",\"startTime\":1733443642,\"endTime\":1733443646},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It''s been really great. And yeah, I hope that we shift, we can shift more that \",\"startTime\":1733443647,\"endTime\":1733443651},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"direction with more and more teachers. Last year there was a lot of, they were \",\"startTime\":1733443651,\"endTime\":1733443655},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443655,\"endTime\":1733443655},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like, no, like teachers were like, no, I''m not doing it. You know, like I don''t \",\"startTime\":1733443655,\"endTime\":1733443659},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"want to slow down for for kids that, you know, like I''m used to teaching. We \",\"startTime\":1733443659,\"endTime\":1733443664},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"have kind of this, we have a, we have a very seasoned staff at this school and we strive for excellence. And that''s really hard to adjust for students that \",\"startTime\":1733443664,\"endTime\":1733443672},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"need that adjustment. So. Yeah, but. \",\"startTime\":1733443672,\"endTime\":1733443677},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Seeing some some great things with the people and I think the team of Gen. Ed \",\"startTime\":1733443678,\"endTime\":1733443682},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"teachers are the right people to be vocal about it, to try to recruit others next year, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443682,\"endTime\":1733443689},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Make such a difference when there''s that buy in and they can shift the culture naturally as a staff, there is nothing harder than when most everybody''s like, oh. \",\"startTime\":1733443690,\"endTime\":1733443698},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Not into it, so that sounds amazing. OK, I''m not. I''m going to break eye contact. \",\"startTime\":1733443700,\"endTime\":1733443704},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443700,\"endTime\":1733443701},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I''m going to like a heavy traffic. \",\"startTime\":1733443704,\"endTime\":1733443708},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"No, you''re fine. You''re actually you''re frozen on my screen, but you I can still \",\"startTime\":1733443709,\"endTime\":1733443713},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"hear you talking, so it''s OK. OK, sounds good. OK, so the question says why \",\"startTime\":1733443713,\"endTime\":1733443717},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, no, OK, I''m in a bad. I''m in a bad part of town. You keep talking. Let''s \",\"startTime\":1733443714,\"endTime\":1733443717},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"go to the next question. Do you want to go first? \",\"startTime\":1733443717,\"endTime\":1733443720},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"do you think inclusion is essential in our schools today? Discuss the impact \",\"startTime\":1733443717,\"endTime\":1733443721},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on students. \",\"startTime\":1733443721,\"endTime\":1733443725},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Since I''m being frozen.\",\"startTime\":1733443731,\"endTime\":1733443732},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Sure, sure. So I would say that this is actually a conversation I had with a \",\"startTime\":1733443733,\"endTime\":1733443737},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"student the other day who is a junior. And we were discussing him being evaluated \",\"startTime\":1733443737,\"endTime\":1733443741},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for an IEP. And he had kind of that typical like, I don''t want to be one of \",\"startTime\":1733443741,\"endTime\":1733443745},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"those students. I don''t want to be in one of those classes. And I was talking \",\"startTime\":1733443745,\"endTime\":1733443750},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"to him and his mom and his counselor was there in our school psych. And I said, \",\"startTime\":1733443750,\"endTime\":1733443754},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you know, you''re you''re the main character in your story. And I was like, who \",\"startTime\":1733443754,\"endTime\":1733443758},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"do you know? \",\"startTime\":1733443758,\"endTime\":1733443762},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"In one of those classes, and he was like, I don''t know anyone. I was like, I \",\"startTime\":1733443763,\"endTime\":1733443767},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"bet you know a lot. I bet you, you know a lot of students that are in classes \",\"startTime\":1733443767,\"endTime\":1733443771},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that have like, I bet you are friends with kids that have Ieps. And I was like, \",\"startTime\":1733443771,\"endTime\":1733443775},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"nobody else is really paying attention to you. I was like, I hate to say it \",\"startTime\":1733443775,\"endTime\":1733443778},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that way, but like you''re the one who thinks everybody''s looking at you and everybody like knows that you''re in that special class. Yeah. I was like, it''s. \",\"startTime\":1733443778,\"endTime\":1733443786},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"You''re not that special.\",\"startTime\":1733443785,\"endTime\":1733443786},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It''s really not the case. And I was like, and you said school has been hard \",\"startTime\":1733443786,\"endTime\":1733443789},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for like 11 years. I was like for. \",\"startTime\":1733443789,\"endTime\":1733443793},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"As long as you can remember, you have not liked school and it''s been difficult. \",\"startTime\":1733443794,\"endTime\":1733443798},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, I want you to graduate and have loved your last few years. Like \",\"startTime\":1733443798,\"endTime\":1733443801},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m sorry that it''s taken this long. But then I talked about our Co Top Model \",\"startTime\":1733443801,\"endTime\":1733443805},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"and his mom started like breaking down in tears and was like, I think this is exactly what he needs, you know? So I think the impact on students is so powerful \",\"startTime\":1733443805,\"endTime\":1733443812},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"and just the fact that they''re just like, no, that kids in my English class not. \",\"startTime\":1733443812,\"endTime\":1733443819},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m, you know, like in a special English class.\",\"startTime\":1733443820,\"endTime\":1733443823},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah, right, right, which is sometimes really sad to like have kids so like separated that just need like resource support. Know some some it''s not even \",\"startTime\":1733443825,\"endTime\":1733443835},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"like the intensive IEP and that many minutes or services that I I love what you said about this. People don''t know and it''s so normalized anymore like when \",\"startTime\":1733443835,\"endTime\":1733443845},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443839,\"endTime\":1733443840},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"some old school parents you talk to think of special education like back in the maybe 90s where people would get. \",\"startTime\":1733443845,\"endTime\":1733443855},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Ton of and you were separated and normalized anymore and we have kids in our school where they''re like, are you pulling me out? Like they get excited like \",\"startTime\":1733443857,\"endTime\":1733443866},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"when when am I going to get pulled out? I want to go with you even with like \",\"startTime\":1733443866,\"endTime\":1733443870},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443870,\"endTime\":1733443870},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"our intervention. We''re like no, honey, you don''t qualify like you don''t need \",\"startTime\":1733443870,\"endTime\":1733443874},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"these extra support, but you know maybe one day we can play for something fun. \",\"startTime\":1733443874,\"endTime\":1733443878},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443876,\"endTime\":1733443877},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"So it''s it''s very accepted and love that. What was the other part when students. \",\"startTime\":1733443878,\"endTime\":1733443882},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443879,\"endTime\":1733443879},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It says discuss its impact on students and why do you think it''s Why do you think inclusion is essential in our schools? \",\"startTime\":1733443886,\"endTime\":1733443893},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yes, I think the other thing I would say too is that everyone has needs and I think the more. \",\"startTime\":1733443896,\"endTime\":1733443901},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Individualized, we can make our educational systems, our processes, our, our teaching, all of those things are better. And so to me, it''s, it''s just how \",\"startTime\":1733443903,\"endTime\":1733443911},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"we should be approaching education. Do we have the resources? No, our schools \",\"startTime\":1733443911,\"endTime\":1733443915},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"aren''t built for that. Our systems aren''t built for that. But I think that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443915,\"endTime\":1733443919},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443918,\"endTime\":1733443919},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"a necessary shift that has to happen as a school system if we''re really honoring every child''s need and their whole self, right? Every, every kid is different \",\"startTime\":1733443919,\"endTime\":1733443927},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"and we have to stop labeling and boxing in. \",\"startTime\":1733443927,\"endTime\":1733443932},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"And to see. And I think it teaches kids that everyone''s different and that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443935,\"endTime\":1733443937},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. \",\"startTime\":1733443937,\"endTime\":1733443939},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"And everyone gets what speed, and that''s OK, which is really important. Oh my \",\"startTime\":1733443939,\"endTime\":1733443942},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443939,\"endTime\":1733443939},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"gosh. \",\"startTime\":1733443942,\"endTime\":1733443944},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m hoping that with this, you know, I don''t know what your school kind of makeup looks like, but we have almost 2000 kids here and we have just this huge yeah, we have this huge increase of 504 plans. And I think a lot of teachers are realizing \",\"startTime\":1733443943,\"endTime\":1733443954},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like I''m just going to make the use of a calculator, a universal support. Like \",\"startTime\":1733443954,\"endTime\":1733443958},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I don''t, I''m so sick of trying to figure out which kids need this and which kids don''t. So I''m kind of hoping the Co teach model is going to shift teachers \",\"startTime\":1733443958,\"endTime\":1733443965},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"thinking too, like this is just a best practice. Like I just need to do this \",\"startTime\":1733443965,\"endTime\":1733443969},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for. \",\"startTime\":1733443969,\"endTime\":1733443973},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1733443974,\"endTime\":1733443975},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All kids, you know, and so that''s where I''m really excited is that I''ve, I''ve seen some teachers that have been here for like 20 years and they''re like opening \",\"startTime\":1733443974,\"endTime\":1733443982},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"up to Co teaching and I think they''re just saying like, oh, that''s not that hard to differentiate that or oh, OK, like that''s how I reteach this, you know, in a different way, or that''s what manipulatives are for or whatever. So I''m \",\"startTime\":1733443982,\"endTime\":1733443994},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m really excited about how it''s impacting the teachers as well. \",\"startTime\":1733443994,\"endTime\":1733443998},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome. And the more access points we can give kids, the better for \",\"startTime\":1733443998,\"endTime\":1733444001},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"them. That''s amazing. We move on to the next question. OK. \",\"startTime\":1733444001,\"endTime\":1733444005},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, sounds good. You know what? It''s it''s like frozen in between on \",\"startTime\":1733444002,\"endTime\":1733444008},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"my screen. I don''t want to put you in danger though, but I can''t see it. \",\"startTime\":1733444008,\"endTime\":1733444014},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, there you go. Do you mind reading it? Sorry.\",\"startTime\":1733444009,\"endTime\":1733444011},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh my gosh. OK, let me get in a safe position here. What do you think is the \",\"startTime\":1733444019,\"endTime\":1733444023},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"hardest part of Co teaching? Share your thoughts and listen to what Mallory \",\"startTime\":1733444023,\"endTime\":1733444028},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"considers the question for you. That''s why I did it. Yeah, it''s for you. So \",\"startTime\":1733444028,\"endTime\":1733444032},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"maybe that''s why it''s a half halfway has your name. \",\"startTime\":1733444032,\"endTime\":1733444036},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, is that what it says?\",\"startTime\":1733444033,\"endTime\":1733444035},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, OK.\",\"startTime\":1733444038,\"endTime\":1733444039},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"That''s interesting, I wonder if mine has your name? Like I only see half of \",\"startTime\":1733444041,\"endTime\":1733444044},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the questions and I think your name is on there too so. \",\"startTime\":1733444044,\"endTime\":1733444047},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, that''s hilarious. OK, maybe. I don''t know.\",\"startTime\":1733444044,\"endTime\":1733444048},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK. I would say the hardest part is probably that beginning part and giving \",\"startTime\":1733444052,\"endTime\":1733444057},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"up, you know, what''s been your space and your, you know, like power, right? \",\"startTime\":1733444057,\"endTime\":1733444062},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And really sharing that. But I also would say that I think after a year or two \",\"startTime\":1733444062,\"endTime\":1733444067},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of doing it, you''re you''re going to see it''s really easier for you. \",\"startTime\":1733444067,\"endTime\":1733444072},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"But I think those initial things at the beginning of like remembering there''s another adult in there and like who, you know, trying to figure out, OK, who''s kind of more in charge this day and when do I take a backseat? I think it''s \",\"startTime\":1733444073,\"endTime\":1733444084},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"it''s been harder for the adults. And then just logistically for our students, \",\"startTime\":1733444084,\"endTime\":1733444087},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"we don''t have enough spots in our Co taught classes. So we''re having to be so \",\"startTime\":1733444087,\"endTime\":1733444091},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"picky about which kids we put in there because we want to stick to a certain ratio. And that''s been really hard too, because if we are seeing more kids could \",\"startTime\":1733444091,\"endTime\":1733444098},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"benefit from it and we don''t have enough space. \",\"startTime\":1733444098,\"endTime\":1733444102},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, right. And likely enough teachers as well. Like if you''re teaching, \",\"startTime\":1733444104,\"endTime\":1733444108},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"if you''re doubling up teachers on a class, that''s one last class during that period that can be taught by somebody else to put more kids in the class. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733444108,\"endTime\":1733444117},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444116,\"endTime\":1733444118},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that''s a hard bread to do. I would agree with your like the setting up the parameters \",\"startTime\":1733444117,\"endTime\":1733444121},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"and boundaries, like what''s my part with your part? How do we cope in real time? \",\"startTime\":1733444121,\"endTime\":1733444125},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"The other challenge with that goes on with that is when teachers are. \",\"startTime\":1733444125,\"endTime\":1733444130},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Fit with each other like how do you support them Co teaching when they''re having conflict because of their teaching style or because of their beliefs around kids or things like that. I think that is something that we can run into it. \",\"startTime\":1733444134,\"endTime\":1733444146},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Nova in the Co teaching model were some some teachers just it was also one of those stuff that works there forever and some of them did not get along and \",\"startTime\":1733444146,\"endTime\":1733444153},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"they would refuse to teach with each other and so then it was always the same teachers Co teaching and then the same that were kind of isolated not doing it so that. \",\"startTime\":1733444153,\"endTime\":1733444164},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"A little bit tricky, but I heard this year they''re doing better. I''m not there \",\"startTime\":1733444167,\"endTime\":1733444170},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"anymore, obviously, but I heard it''s got yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733444170,\"endTime\":1733444173},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right, Yeah, I think you bring up a really good point. We had a bad pairing \",\"startTime\":1733444172,\"endTime\":1733444175},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"last year and they''re not Co teaching at all this year. Like we didn''t feel \",\"startTime\":1733444175,\"endTime\":1733444179},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like they''d be a good fit for anybody after the year that they had together and probably they were both turned off from teaching in the in the in the end, so. \",\"startTime\":1733444179,\"endTime\":1733444189},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444186,\"endTime\":1733444188},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, they taught just I think it was only one class that was like a Co taught math and. \",\"startTime\":1733444191,\"endTime\":1733444198},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Did they did they teach the entire year or just a couple of classes?\",\"startTime\":1733444193,\"endTime\":1733444198},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It was they were paired together before I was in this building and I, I didn''t agree with the pairing once I found out the reason, But neither one of them were very strong teachers. And so the rationale was, well, let''s put them both \",\"startTime\":1733444205,\"endTime\":1733444216},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"together and together, maybe they could bring out each other''s like strengths. \",\"startTime\":1733444216,\"endTime\":1733444220},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So I kind of understand that, but like, I think you need your very best teachers for a Co Top Model, not your ones that are struggling the most. And so I, I \",\"startTime\":1733444220,\"endTime\":1733444228},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yes.\",\"startTime\":1733444226,\"endTime\":1733444226},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"think if you got a math teacher who''s not that great at teaching math, and then you''ve got a special Ed teacher who just like. \",\"startTime\":1733444228,\"endTime\":1733444235},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444229,\"endTime\":1733444230},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Wants to do their own thing. You run into some real power dynamics, like with \",\"startTime\":1733444237,\"endTime\":1733444240},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the with the. So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733444240,\"endTime\":1733444244},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that makes a lot of sense. And their own insecurities. So the things that \",\"startTime\":1733444245,\"endTime\":1733444249},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"they''re not good at that they''re working on are amplified at times. Oh yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733444249,\"endTime\":1733444253},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, and they were both very respectful to one another. But I think it was \",\"startTime\":1733444251,\"endTime\":1733444255},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that''s, that''s hard. OK. \",\"startTime\":1733444253,\"endTime\":1733444256},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"pretty quickly, like our special Ed teacher kind of turned into a para in that space, and it was just kind of insulting, you know? So, alright. \",\"startTime\":1733444255,\"endTime\":1733444263}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.472548+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.472548+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 909, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.240Z", "session_title": "Coteaching improves inclusion", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "56", "name": "Coteaching improves inclusion", "tags": [{"name": "Inclusion"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
