	('ee4301d4-780a-4c5b-bb0b-6ef59f10bb8f', 'a978d068-04bc-45ac-b24c-f6e367bb9007', '135714', '"[{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Good morning.\",\"startTime\":1734446849,\"endTime\":1734446850},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Are you and I the only ones that sign in in the morning?\",\"startTime\":1734446851,\"endTime\":1734446853},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"It can''t be. It can''t be. And of course I''m driving. I am. I''m running late \",\"startTime\":1734446855,\"endTime\":1734446859},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"today. \",\"startTime\":1734446859,\"endTime\":1734446863},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I see you''re driving this morning also.\",\"startTime\":1734446859,\"endTime\":1734446861},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"So so anyway, so we get started, then what do we got? Ice Breakers share conversation \",\"startTime\":1734446868,\"endTime\":1734446873},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Sure.\",\"startTime\":1734446872,\"endTime\":1734446873},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"you''ve had lately. \",\"startTime\":1734446873,\"endTime\":1734446879},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"What''s the same? OK.\",\"startTime\":1734446886,\"endTime\":1734446888},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Foster trust and psychological safety during data conversations.\",\"startTime\":1734446893,\"endTime\":1734446897},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I use a protocol from a watch. What''s that website?\",\"startTime\":1734446904,\"endTime\":1734446908},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I can never remember the name of it. Like learning forward or something like \",\"startTime\":1734446913,\"endTime\":1734446915},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"that. \",\"startTime\":1734446915,\"endTime\":1734446917},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"It''s the Atlas protocol. Do you ever do that one? The Atlas Data protocol?\",\"startTime\":1734446920,\"endTime\":1734446923},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Tell me what it is. I don''t know it by that name.\",\"startTime\":1734446927,\"endTime\":1734446929},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"It''s the Atlas data analysis protocol. When you divide up into groups and there''s \",\"startTime\":1734446932,\"endTime\":1734446937},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"a couple of steps to the first step is that you simply list the facts that you see in the data and you spend about 10 minutes just listing the facts. And the \",\"startTime\":1734446937,\"endTime\":1734446946},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734446946,\"endTime\":1734446946},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"next step is interpretation of the data and then. \",\"startTime\":1734446946,\"endTime\":1734446951},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"The third step is.\",\"startTime\":1734446954,\"endTime\":1734446955},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"What you know that implications of the data. So by dividing up and pulling out \",\"startTime\":1734446957,\"endTime\":1734446962},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"that the interpretation of the data from the facts of the data, you, you kind of separate out the the blame, the shame and blame part of it, which I think helps. How about you? \",\"startTime\":1734446962,\"endTime\":1734446976},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep.\",\"startTime\":1734446979,\"endTime\":1734446979},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it''s hard. We use a ton of different ones.\",\"startTime\":1734446981,\"endTime\":1734446985},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I had a teacher get mad at me yesterday because she had emailed me questions and I talked to her and emailed me questions. So she said she was you never \",\"startTime\":1734446989,\"endTime\":1734446996},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"tell me it was on great distribution pattern broken down by class and by teacher. \",\"startTime\":1734446996,\"endTime\":1734447000},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"She''s like, it''s not fair that you''re counting kids with absence is against me. And then she put in her e-mail, They''re wasting my time and I''m wasting \",\"startTime\":1734447000,\"endTime\":1734447008},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"their time. So then I. \",\"startTime\":1734447008,\"endTime\":1734447012},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Replied back with a trebuchet of Hattie''s research on teacher efficacy and belief in students and Pygmalion effect, and she didn''t like that at all. \",\"startTime\":1734447014,\"endTime\":1734447027},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I''m like all you do is complain about your kids. So we''re not going to desegregate \",\"startTime\":1734447033,\"endTime\":1734447038},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I''ve had to do well, and at some point in time she has to say, OK, you can only work with what you have control over and which is your behavior. So what is \",\"startTime\":1734447033,\"endTime\":1734447039},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"out our gifted kids from our 504 kids from our eel kids from our kids who aren''t there. Kids are kids now. It''s not fair to compare English 3 to pre AP or American \",\"startTime\":1734447038,\"endTime\":1734447049},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"it about your behavior that might be contributing to whatever it is you''re talking about, right? \",\"startTime\":1734447039,\"endTime\":1734447045},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"lit to AP lit. That''s not a fair comparison. But. \",\"startTime\":1734447049,\"endTime\":1734447054},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep.\",\"startTime\":1734447069,\"endTime\":1734447069},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"But she doesn''t see that she''s doing anything less than perfection. She''s a \",\"startTime\":1734447071,\"endTime\":1734447075},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"veteran teacher. She''s fine. She''s just in that 24th year, 23rd year. Kids have \",\"startTime\":1734447075,\"endTime\":1734447079},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"changed. \",\"startTime\":1734447079,\"endTime\":1734447082},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734447085,\"endTime\":1734447085},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"We got old. All right, next one.\",\"startTime\":1734447091,\"endTime\":1734447094},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"That''s alright.\",\"startTime\":1734447097,\"endTime\":1734447099},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Just so you know, I''m going to go through this part where I lose cell service for about 15 seconds. What strategies do you enjoy to foster trust? Consider \",\"startTime\":1734447100,\"endTime\":1734447110},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1734447107,\"endTime\":1734447108},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"examples like using growth mindset language. \",\"startTime\":1734447110,\"endTime\":1734447115},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Sharing clear next step importance of listening Reflect on you''ve done to foster trust in your school''s data processes. \",\"startTime\":1734447124,\"endTime\":1734447135},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"All right, what have you done, friends?\",\"startTime\":1734447139,\"endTime\":1734447141},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I think one of the key ones, I think one of the key ones is making sure you have accurate data and we struggle with that sometimes. \",\"startTime\":1734447140,\"endTime\":1734447149},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Because like when we turn in our graduate to the district, they don''t always fix the P210. We had it happen in the class of 23 where the district put the \",\"startTime\":1734447153,\"endTime\":1734447166},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"wrong grad date in the system. So one of our schools had a 0% graduate. \",\"startTime\":1734447166,\"endTime\":1734447172},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"And there''s some some little things like that that are super frustrating outside our control, so we shouldn''t complain about them, but still super frustrating. \",\"startTime\":1734447178,\"endTime\":1734447187},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734447192,\"endTime\":1734447192}