ge and our great distribution pattern for freshmen we''re sitting well at quarter, we''re at 93% pass rate which is pre COVID numbers for us which was nice. \",\"startTime\":1734447367,\"endTime\":1734447386},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I just, I just don''t see the any good, umm, looking at SBA data that just tells you, you know, you suck doesn''t help us. \",\"startTime\":1734447390,\"endTime\":1734447399},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I worry for SBA data because the test is no longer required and high schoolers aren''t going to give best effort or even take the junior year test that isn''t required. \",\"startTime\":1734447403,\"endTime\":1734447414},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Exactly. Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1734447416,\"endTime\":1734447418},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"And the the state needs to take ownership of that. Again, I''m complaining about \",\"startTime\":1734447419,\"endTime\":1734447423},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"things outside my control, but the state needs to take ownership that if they''ve made nine different pathways, and some of the pathways are pretty freaking easy. \",\"startTime\":1734447423,\"endTime\":1734447432},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Why would kids come on? We do a late start. Why would kids come and or give \",\"startTime\":1734447433,\"endTime\":1734447438},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"best effort when they know they can get it a different way? \",\"startTime\":1734447438,\"endTime\":1734447443},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Exactly. Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1734447445,\"endTime\":1734447446},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"All right. Do we have more questions this morning?\",\"startTime\":1734447451,\"endTime\":1734447453},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I don''t know, I''m pulling in to get my coffee.\",\"startTime\":1734447456,\"endTime\":1734447462},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Hold on.\",\"startTime\":1734447462,\"endTime\":1734447463},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep. How do you reframe data to focus on improvement rather than blame?\",\"startTime\":1734447468,\"endTime\":1734447473},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"List of the norm. I mean, first of all, when we look at data, I, I flat out \",\"startTime\":1734447472,\"endTime\":1734447476},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"say that we''re not about shame or blame. That doesn''t help anyone. So I actually \",\"startTime\":1734447476,\"endTime\":1734447480},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"put that out there as one of our norms. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734447480,\"endTime\":1734447484},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Although sometimes a little peer pressure if you''re the outlier isn''t a bad thing. \",\"startTime\":1734447501,\"endTime\":1734447505},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Why do kids fail your class at just partially high rates?\",\"startTime\":1734447510,\"endTime\":1734447512},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I put that pressure on though, in terms of how I disseminate the data, whether I''m going to attach names to it or not attach names to it. And so being \",\"startTime\":1734447515,\"endTime\":1734447524},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"strategic in the data that I put out and how I how I put it out into what groups I put it out and what groups teachers are in when I put it out, I think all of those pieces are very strategic. Am I going to give the data to the teachers \",\"startTime\":1734447524,\"endTime\":1734447537},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"in their place? \",\"startTime\":1734447537,\"endTime\":1734447542},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Who''s going to facilitate the discussion?\",\"startTime\":1734447544,\"endTime\":1734447546},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Is it have all of that helps, you know, frame what I''m going to do. So I''ll \",\"startTime\":1734447547,\"endTime\":1734447551},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"give great, great distribution data out, but I''ll give that to the PLCS and I''ll have the 