\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yep, Yep, we''re experiencing that now. So it''s all good, though we''ll, we''ll \",\"startTime\":1736261216,\"endTime\":1736261220},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"figure it out sooner or later, sooner or later. So you ready? That''s the next \",\"startTime\":1736261220,\"endTime\":1736261225},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, alright.\",\"startTime\":1736261225,\"endTime\":1736261226},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"one. \",\"startTime\":1736261225,\"endTime\":1736261229},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Hit next. There we go. Oh, no. Hit. Hit next. Hit next. Down below. There we \",\"startTime\":1736261232,\"endTime\":1736261237},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Ready. Alright, Favorite family?\",\"startTime\":1736261237,\"endTime\":1736261239},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"go. There we go. Awesome. This is so cool. I''m just so glad I''m getting Heidi \",\"startTime\":1736261237,\"endTime\":1736261243},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Mauer this morning. I love it, love it, love it. Hope you''re still there. You \",\"startTime\":1736261243,\"endTime\":1736261248},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"still there? OK, OK. I said no, that''s OK. I just said it''s, it''s so cool to \",\"startTime\":1736261248,\"endTime\":1736261253},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Uh, alright Valerie, I''m back. Yeah, yeah, I have a Internet dead zone on my \",\"startTime\":1736261248,\"endTime\":1736261252},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"way. How? \",\"startTime\":1736261252,\"endTime\":1736261257},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"have Heidi Meyer this morning. I''ll, I''ll read the question for you. \",\"startTime\":1736261253,\"endTime\":1736261259},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How can schools bridge? How can schools bridge the knowledge gap for families \",\"startTime\":1736261277,\"endTime\":1736261281},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261279,\"endTime\":1736261279},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"unfamiliar with the high school to college or trade pipeline or pathway? \",\"startTime\":1736261281,\"endTime\":1736261285},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We ironically, we''ve been having some conversations about we do the normal parent night and they''re inviting the the families in. But really what we''re finding \",\"startTime\":1736261297,\"endTime\":1736261307},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"is the kids get the majority of the information from the schools, not their parents. So we''re targeting the kids more than we are the families. \",\"startTime\":1736261307,\"endTime\":1736261317},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And, you know, inviting the parents along for the ride, that really targeting the kids more than the families. \",\"startTime\":1736261322,\"endTime\":1736261328},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, right, right. Oh, I I don''t know either. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261324,\"endTime\":1736261331},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I don''t know if that''s bad.\",\"startTime\":1736261330,\"endTime\":1736261331},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"But we''ve got some news. We have a weekly newsletter that goes out from our \",\"startTime\":1736261337,\"endTime\":1736261341},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"college to career counselor, and it has all the scholarships and deadlines and information. And the kids are just saying it''s so much information that it''s \",\"startTime\":1736261341,\"endTime\":1736261350},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"too much to digest. And they they were. \",\"startTime\":1736261350,\"endTime\":1736261354},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Getting it. I freeze again. I keep freezing. Internet around here is horrible. \",\"startTime\":1736261368,\"endTime\":1736261374},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Gotcha. No, we''re you''re in and out. That''s OK. Yeah. No, no, you''re Yeah, No, \",\"startTime\":1736261369,\"endTime\":1736261373},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I got that. The advisory, advisory programs. Yeah. And that and that makes sense, \",\"startTime\":1736261373,\"endTime\":1736261377},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"especially if it''s built, especially if it''s built into the school day. You \",\"startTime\":1736261377,\"endTime\":1736261382},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261378,\"endTime\":1736261378},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"know, I think about if if I was back in a building now and this knowledge gap for families and people unfamiliar. \",\"startTime\":1736261382,\"endTime\":1736261390},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"So so parent, so paranoid, but the kids wanted more advisory and stuff.\",\"startTime\":1736261382,\"endTime\":1736261386},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, it starts before high school. And how do you build a build a system \",\"startTime\":1736261399,\"endTime\":1736261404},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"that that that shares those opportunities, not just at the school setting, but community wide? How do you integrate into and use some community stakeholder \",\"startTime\":1736261404,\"endTime\":1736261414},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"organizations that interface with, with parents who may not know what''s possible for their kids? And yes, kids, kids get all the information at school and and \",\"startTime\":1736261414,\"endTime\":1736261424},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"like you said, feel inundated with some of that stuff, but is there? \",\"startTime\":1736261424,\"endTime\":1736261429},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is there a different way to engage families, to provide some knowledge for them? \",\"startTime\":1736261429,\"endTime\":1736261433},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Because it is you''ve, you''re going through it. You''ll go through it here again. \",\"startTime\":1736261433,\"endTime\":1736261436},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But even though I''ve worked in schools, you worked in schools, I didn''t even understand half the things that were available for my own kids. And s