\":1734449769,\"endTime\":1734449773},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I just need to be focused and that stuff done.\",\"startTime\":1734449774,\"endTime\":1734449777}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.182681+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.182681+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 212, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.114Z", "session_title": "AI for Educators: Applying AI in Your Job", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "196", "name": "AI for Educators: Applying AI in Your Job", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('04ffa665-b08e-4b3e-9678-770242ad18ad', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', '136593', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Let me mute this.\",\"startTime\":1738002387,\"endTime\":1738002389},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1738002391,\"endTime\":1738002391},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yay, you hear me? OK.\",\"startTime\":1738002391,\"endTime\":1738002396},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I can loud and clear.\",\"startTime\":1738002394,\"endTime\":1738002396},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Sweet, sweet, sweet. Oh, and we are in AI learning tools. Yes, we made it.\",\"startTime\":1738002397,\"endTime\":1738002402},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Sweet, sweet. OK, great. Your partner Dale. Hello, Dale and Ice Baker. What''s \",\"startTime\":1738002403,\"endTime\":1738002409},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Fantastic.\",\"startTime\":1738002403,\"endTime\":1738002404},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"your favorite book or movie that features futuristic technology and why? \",\"startTime\":1738002409,\"endTime\":1738002414},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I like Dune was a really interesting, It''s a really fascinating concept. I remember \",\"startTime\":1738002416,\"endTime\":1738002421},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"reading the book a long time ago and just being like fascinated by. \",\"startTime\":1738002421,\"endTime\":1738002426},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"A world of no water or or or like the value of that water. Yeah. And processing \",\"startTime\":1738002427,\"endTime\":1738002431},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"it in that way. So, yeah, I would say like Dune was a was a fascinating book \",\"startTime\":1738002431,\"endTime\":1738002435},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"for me. What about you? \",\"startTime\":1738002435,\"endTime\":1738002439},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s a good one. The Matrix gets my brain all in a buzz.\",\"startTime\":1738002440,\"endTime\":1738002447},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Just because of that, being able to connect into our neurology and.\",\"startTime\":1738002448,\"endTime\":1738002453},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"To have some of that time like of what''s going on, and I know that doesn''t work that way, but something magical about downloading the ability to fly a helicopter or something instantly. \",\"startTime\":1738002454,\"endTime\":1738002466},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002467,\"endTime\":1738002468},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002469,\"endTime\":1738002470},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But that, yeah, that that movie was one that just made my brain think pretty hard about stuff like that. \",\"startTime\":1738002471,\"endTime\":1738002477},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Awesome. So we we go on to the next prompt. Partner ready, OK.\",\"startTime\":1738002478,\"endTime\":1738002482},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah. Partner ready.\",\"startTime\":1738002481,\"endTime\":1738002484},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Oh, would you like me to go first?\",\"startTime\":1738002486,\"endTime\":1738002488},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"How has?\",\"startTime\":1738002487,\"endTime\":1738002488},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Because mine says ask Dale, I''m guessing does your say ask Jeff?\",\"startTime\":1738002489,\"endTime\":1738002492},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"It just says share first.\",\"startTime\":1738002493,\"endTime\":1738002495},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, OK, so ask Dale.\",\"startTime\":1738002495,\"endTime\":1738002497},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"How has AI changed your work as an educator or leader of educators so far?\",\"startTime\":1738002497,\"endTime\":1738002504},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Look, it''s.\",\"startTime\":1738002508,\"endTime\":1738002510},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"It''s totally changed the way that I work, I would say.\",\"startTime\":1738002512,\"endTime\":1738002517},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"The umm a large part of the compliance of my job and different paperwork, elements of my job and my ability to differentiate across different classes and grades. \",\"startTime\":1738002519,\"endTime\":1738002531},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Umm, and do that in in such a like a a, a ramped up way has totally changed the way that I. \",\"startTime\":1738002531,\"endTime\":1738002540},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"And them able to present myself to kids and to be really present in.\",\"startTime\":1738002541,\"endTime\":1738002547},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"The most important stuff of my job. So yeah, I, I would say it''s had a massive \",\"startTime\":1738002547,\"endTime\":1738002550},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"impact on, on what I do. \",\"startTime\":1738002550,\"endTime\":1738002553},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Wow, give me more detail. Like what''s 1 area that you''d say is massive impact? \",\"startTime\":1738002555,\"endTime\":1738002560},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it''s my ability to differentiate for different students. Umm.\",\"startTime\":1738002561,\"endTime\":1738002566},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Within minutes of seeing either lessons or a lesson that I walked into or.\",\"startTime\":1738002570,\"endTime\":1738002577},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"When I''m interacting with a student with with a text or with a math or or.\",\"startTime\":1738002580,\"endTime\":1738002587},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Something that my student is struggling with or needs accessibility points into to engage with this task. I''m able to differentiate it. \",\"startTime\":1738002588,\"endTime\":1738002598},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"In such a fast and accurate way that that then allows my students to have different entry points into. \",\"startTime\":1738002599,\"endTime\":1738002607},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That new learning.\",\"startTime\":1738002607,\"endTime\":1738002608},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That seems so efficient.\",\"startTime\":1738002611,\"endTime\":1738002612},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Having a tool to be able to get those differentiations right away.\",\"startTime\":1738002614,\"endTime\":1738002617},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s pretty cool.\",\"startTime\":1738002617,\"endTime\":1738002618},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002619,\"endTime\":1738002619},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, that''s mine just says ask you and then yours. Yours says share.\",\"startTime\":1738002622,\"endTime\":1738002627},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, mine says. I mentioned specific AI tools and look, I''ve looked at different \",\"startTime\":1738002626,\"endTime\":1738002630},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"tools and I know it seems like. \",\"startTime\":1738002630,\"endTime\":1738002634},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Every week there''s new tools, right that who can the new AI tools, they can do different things and I''m I''m certain that all of them have amazing value or, or or value in different ways, but. \",\"startTime\":1738002635,\"endTime\":1738002646},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I started to create.\",\"startTime\":1738002649,\"endTime\":1738002653},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"GPT. So in Chat GPTS, I create an account. I created individual GPTS for individual \",\"startTime\":1738002653,\"endTime\":1738002658},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"tasks that I have in my job that sort of take up the biggest volume of time. \",\"startTime\":1738002658,\"endTime\":1738002664},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So I''ve been really focused on creating Chat GPTS and then training those GPTS over the last year to get the information that I want in the format that I want, in the tone and voice that I want. So yeah, it''s been very much. \",\"startTime\":1738002664,\"endTime\":1738002682},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Or ChatGPT.\",\"startTime\":1738002683,\"endTime\":1738002683},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I like it. Tell me more about the training. How are you doing the training of \",\"startTime\":1738002684,\"endTime\":1738002687},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the GPTS to get what you want? \",\"startTime\":1738002687,\"endTime\":1738002689},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, you know, like I''m when I ask her questions.\",\"startTime\":1738002690,\"endTime\":1738002693},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Well, first of all, setting it up is a key part is like you''re saying, OK, I want you to be an expert in this, this, this and this. I want you to. \",\"startTime\":1738002694,\"endTime\":1738002702},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Learn or or focus on information from these different resources, right?\",\"startTime\":1738002704,\"endTime\":1738002709},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"As a special educator, that might be the idea in Wisconsin, it''s the Wisconsin State standards, OK, So I need it to be pulling from those resources and be an expert there. And I needed to give it to me in a tone that is suitable for \",\"startTime\":1738002710,\"endTime\":1738002722},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"student centered learning. I, I need it in El education, which is the model \",\"startTime\":1738002722,\"endTime\":1738002726},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"that I work in, or I need it to consider the sort of the deeper learning platform. \",\"startTime\":1738002726,\"endTime\":1738002731},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So I''m saying. \",\"startTime\":1738002731,\"endTime\":1738002735},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Give me this information, give it to me in the format that I want from the resources that I believe in and I know to be true and the in the, in the sort of voice and the tone that is most suitable for for my students. So over time, you, you, \",\"startTime\":1738002736,\"endTime\":1738002750},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"you sort of train out or do your best to train out the bias in the information that you''ve got or the different. \",\"startTime\":1738002750,\"endTime\":1738002760},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"It starts to understand what you''re looking for and the formats that you''re looking for and in the voice that you''re looking for. \",\"startTime\":1738002761,\"endTime\":1738002768},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So that that''s what I mean by train.\",\"startTime\":1738002768,\"endTime\":1738002770},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Are you noticing that just by using it, it gets better at doing what it''s doing because you give it feedback on how you want things even after the original setup? \",\"startTime\":1738002770,\"endTime\":1738002780},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yes, I had an instant saw last week where I worked on this thing for a couple of hours to create. \",\"startTime\":1738002780,\"endTime\":1738002786},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"My minutes where I could just put in minutes.\",\"startTime\":1738002787,\"endTime\":1738002789},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"And be able to transfer that into a format and a line item that is in for compliance. \",\"startTime\":1738002790,\"endTime\":1738002798},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That traditionally took me a long time to do, and now?\",\"startTime\":1738002798,\"endTime\":1738002803},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Now it gives it to me after quite a bit of work. It gives it to me in the format \",\"startTime\":1738002804,\"endTime\":1738002808},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"that I want. So I''m able to just put very quickly, put in information in there \",\"startTime\":1738002808,\"endTime\":1738002811},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"at different intervals and then say, hey, I need you to, you know, in the format that I want, compiled all the information. \",\"startTime\":1738002811,\"endTime\":1738002818},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"In my preferred template go, you know, for whatever date period go and then it just goes bang. I just copy paste it into a compliance document and I''m done. \",\"startTime\":1738002819,\"endTime\":1738002828},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome. That''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1738002830,\"endTime\":1738002832},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Uh, OK, I''m gonna hit next and unless you''ve got more, that''s that''s way cool. \",\"startTime\":1738002833,\"endTime\":1738002839},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Big turn sharing with Dale. How do you think AI will change the role of learners \",\"startTime\":1738002845,\"endTime\":1738002848},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in the future? \",\"startTime\":1738002848,\"endTime\":1738002850},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"One I think like what you were just saying, I was doing similar roles with using GP TS and creating them. And by the way I gave many of my GP TS names like I \",\"startTime\":1738002854,\"endTime\":1738002861},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"have cuddles. \",\"startTime\":1738002861,\"endTime\":1738002864},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Cuddles is a cuttlefish and Cuddles is my business consultant with all of my docs for my personal business stuff. And this helps me to know which GPT to \",\"startTime\":1738002864,\"endTime\":1738002873},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"talk to. At times they''re like, Oh yeah, talk to Cuddles. \",\"startTime\":1738002873,\"endTime\":1738002878},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But that how to start it up and get it moving forward. I think for students \",\"startTime\":1738002879,\"endTime\":1738002884},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"similarly about giving them the tools to create GP T. \",\"startTime\":1738002884,\"endTime\":1738002889},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"As assistance to do the work that they want to do. So if their project is something \",\"startTime\":1738002892,\"endTime\":1738002897},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"about skateboarding ramps, for example, I want to build skateboard ramps because that''s what I''m excited about. They might build their GP TS to do the different \",\"startTime\":1738002897,\"endTime\":1738002906},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"components around whether it''s the engineering of that or the the procurement of resources or the liabilities of it or the. \",\"startTime\":1738002906,\"endTime\":1738002915},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Maintenance or whatever it might be, but they''ll have to start becoming creative of thinking. \",\"startTime\":1738002916,\"endTime\":1738002922},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"How do I use these tools? In particular, how do I create assistance that will \",\"startTime\":1738002922,\"endTime\":1738002927},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"help me do what I want to do to reach my bigger project? \",\"startTime\":1738002927,\"endTime\":1738002931},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So I think it''s going to change the role of learners and what they''re doing as it will give them more power to do things and to create assistance, like what you''re saying, to expedite and become efficient with the work that they''re doing. I see that as a real, real key. And, and again, that''s like level 2 and \",\"startTime\":1738002932,\"endTime\":1738002948},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"MMM, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002947,\"endTime\":1738002947},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"3 users of, of AI tools, But that, that''s what I see right away is that that students, learners in general that we''re going to be thinking, oh, how? \",\"startTime\":1738002948,\"endTime\":1738002957},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"How do I get myself an assistant to help?\",\"startTime\":1738002959,\"endTime\":1738002961},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Become more efficient and get just get the tedious stuff done fast.\",\"startTime\":1738002962,\"endTime\":1738002966},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002963,\"endTime\":1738002963},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s really interesting, Jeff, that mindset.\",\"startTime\":1738002966,\"endTime\":1738002969},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Like of what it can do and like what I can, what it can help me achieve I guess and learn. \",\"startTime\":1738002972,\"endTime\":1738002978},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I think that mindset is a big shift for adults and probably it''s probably not that big a shift for kids. They they kids adapt and learn really, really quickly. \",\"startTime\":1738002979,\"endTime\":1738002989},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738002990,\"endTime\":1738002991},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Uponting the mindset around AI and different tools are really slow progression for a lot of adults. Some are early adopters. They''re like, Oh yeah, this can \",\"startTime\":1738002991,\"endTime\":1738002998},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"this, this is really helpful. I can use this immediately to do this, this and \",\"startTime\":1738002998,\"endTime\":1738003002},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"this. \",\"startTime\":1738003002,\"endTime\":1738003006},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"And and other sort of new learners are a little bit like, oh, that seems.\",\"startTime\":1738003006,\"endTime\":1738003011},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Like, uh.\",\"startTime\":1738003013,\"endTime\":1738003014},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"They sort of zone, they sort of zoom back and they''re like, oh, I don''t know if this is the right way and what are the implications to this? And like, there''s \",\"startTime\":1738003014,\"endTime\":1738003021},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"there, but I feel like. \",\"startTime\":1738003021,\"endTime\":1738003024},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"There''s a there''s a mindset shift that has to occur.\",\"startTime\":1738003027,\"endTime\":1738003031},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So adult learners are now teachers and people who are.\",\"startTime\":1738003032,\"endTime\":1738003036},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Who can anyone can use this you know to to be creative and save some self save themselves time and learn. \",\"startTime\":1738003037,\"endTime\":1738003043},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"But that''s a the, the mindset shift is a really interesting one for for adult learners, I think. \",\"startTime\":1738003044,\"endTime\":1738003051},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I think even for younger students who grow up and adults who have grown up in spoon feeding, sit still and and I''ll tell you Dale, how to do it. Just \",\"startTime\":1738003053,\"endTime\":1738003065},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"take the nose and when we are in that. \",\"startTime\":1738003065,\"endTime\":1738003069},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Non creative, non owning of our learning. When I don''t own my learning and I''m \",\"startTime\":1738003069,\"endTime\":1738003074},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"not the one at the driver''s seat for what I''m doing and I''m waiting for somebody else to tell me what to do, then I will become more and more stressed about doing this because it does require creativity. And, and as you were talking, \",\"startTime\":1738003074,\"endTime\":1738003086},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it made me think about there''s that math practice standard about using appropriate tools strategically. And that means that kids would need and learners would \",\"startTime\":1738003086,\"endTime\":1738003094},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"need choice. \",\"startTime\":1738003094,\"endTime\":1738003098},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"To use appropriate tools strategically, you have to have a bunch of tools on the table and have a need for using tools. And that''s a messy, chaotic place. \",\"startTime\":1738003100,\"endTime\":1738003108},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And for many of us, we don''t like that. And so for my point is if if you have \",\"startTime\":1738003108,\"endTime\":1738003112},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yep, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738003109,\"endTime\":1738003111},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"grown up or you''ve been in that special Ed is typically this, which is sad. \",\"startTime\":1738003112,\"endTime\":1738003117},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Let me just feed you now and just wait. I''ll be with you in a minute. Dale, \",\"startTime\":1738003117,\"endTime\":1738003121},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"don''t do anything yet. I''ll be over there in a minute to show you how to do \",\"startTime\":1738003121,\"endTime\":1738003125},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it. \",\"startTime\":1738003125,\"endTime\":1738003129},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"If that''s the case, then you''re not authentically being a human being who''s autonomous, and how do we cultivate that? So I think the role of learners, as \",\"startTime\":1738003130,\"endTime\":1738003139},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you said, is much around helping them become the independent. \",\"startTime\":1738003139,\"endTime\":1738003143},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Learner that they need to be in supporting them along the way and their role will be ownership more and more ownership. What assistance do they need? What \",\"startTime\":1738003145,\"endTime\":1738003152},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"tutors do they do they need like I''m hearing. \",\"startTime\":1738003152,\"endTime\":1738003155},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738003156,\"endTime\":1738003156},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I read from Mike, he had a feedback from one of his students earlier this week and it was saying that the student is using AI tools as its his own tutor. When \",\"startTime\":1738003156,\"endTime\":1738003166},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"he goes home he''s having it help teach him and he''s like. \",\"startTime\":1738003166,\"endTime\":1738003170},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That I can access a teacher is what he was calling it. That I don''t need my. \",\"startTime\":1738003172,\"endTime\":1738003177},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Classroom teacher, I can go and get these other teachers, and I''ve heard from other people too, teachers as well, that as they''re supporting their students, they''re like, I don''t know all of this stuff, man. So I''m going online and I''m \",\"startTime\":1738003178,\"endTime\":1738003189},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"having the AI to help me learn about whatever it was that they needed to help learn to help their students. \",\"startTime\":1738003189,\"endTime\":1738003197},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So there, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738003197,\"endTime\":1738003198},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That is, I mean, that is, that''s a really.\",\"startTime\":1738003198,\"endTime\":1738003201},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That''s a really interesting.\",\"startTime\":1738003201,\"endTime\":1738003202},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"A really interesting option and.\",\"startTime\":1738003205,\"endTime\":1738003208},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That will be like, there''s a lot of in the environment that I work, there''s a lot of concern about the way kids are using it, even even the way the teachers are using it and. \",\"startTime\":1738003211,\"endTime\":1738003221},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That''s an excellent example of a really creative and positive way that students can really benefit from their use of of a tool. \",\"startTime\":1738003222,\"endTime\":1738003234},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Like this or like, you know, ChatGPT for example, they were talking about before. \",\"startTime\":1738003234,\"endTime\":1738003237},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That''s that''s super interesting. \",\"startTime\":1738003237,\"endTime\":1738003240},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''ll, I''ll send you that quote from Mike''s kid. It was, it was wonderful \",\"startTime\":1738003241,\"endTime\":1738003244},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to see